window.MOCK_DATA={"version":"coherent-contrast-1","questions":[{"id":"x101","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Customer and sponsor","prompt":"Which role defines service requirements and is accountable for the outcomes of consuming the service?","options":["Customer","Sponsor","User","Service provider"],"why":"The customer defines requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. The sponsor authorizes the budget; the user uses the service. One person may hold several roles.","hook":"Requirements and outcomes: customer. Budget: sponsor.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Customer bepaalt eisen en draagt verantwoordelijkheid voor outcomes. Sponsor autoriseert het budget; user gebruikt de service. De provider levert. Kijk naar de beschreven verantwoordelijkheid, niet naar de senioriteit of functietitel. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen combineren.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x102","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service management","prompt":"Which description defines service management?","options":["Specialized organizational capabilities for enabling customer value through services","Joint activities by a provider and consumer to maintain their service relationship","A set of connected activities used to deliver a product or service to a consumer","An organization's resources designed to perform work or achieve an objective"],"why":"Service management concerns specialized capabilities for enabling value through services. The other descriptions point toward relationship management, a value stream and a practice.","hook":"Service management: capabilities that enable value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Service management betreft gespecialiseerde capaciteiten voor klantwaarde via services. Gezamenlijke provider-consumentactiviteiten beschrijven relatiebeheer. Een verbonden werkstroom is iets anders; een set middelen voor een doel is een practice. De brede organisatorische capaciteit is hier bepalend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x103","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] describes assurance that a product or service will meet agreed requirements.","options":["Warranty","Utility","Value","Outcome"],"why":"Warranty is assurance that agreed requirements will be met, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Utility concerns the functionality offered.","hook":"Warranty: can I rely on it?","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Warranty is de zekerheid dat afgesproken eisen aan gebruik worden gehaald, bijvoorbeeld beschikbaarheid en capaciteit. Utility is benodigde functionaliteit. Value is ervaren nut; outcome is het bereikte stakeholderresultaat. Alleen de aanwezigheid van functies bewijst geen betrouwbare bruikbaarheid.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"missing-word"},{"id":"x104","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service","prompt":"Which description best defines a service?","options":["A means of enabling joint value creation by helping customers achieve outcomes without managing specific costs and risks","A combination of organizational resources designed to provide value to a consumer","A description of one or more services addressing a target consumer group's needs","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by carrying out an activity"],"why":"A service helps customers achieve outcomes while the provider takes on specific costs and risks. The alternatives describe a product, a service offering and an output.","hook":"Service: desired outcomes with specific burdens handled for you.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een service helpt klanten outcomes te bereiken zonder bepaalde specifieke kosten en risico's zelf te beheren. Dat betekent niet dat alle klantverantwoordelijkheid verdwijnt. Middelen configureren beschrijft een product, de formele propositie een offering en een oplevering een output.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x105","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Output and outcome","prompt":"A reporting service produces a daily stock report. Store managers use it to reduce shortages. Which pairing is correct?","options":["Daily report: output; fewer shortages: outcome","Daily report: outcome; fewer shortages: output","Daily report: warranty; fewer shortages: utility","Daily report: utility; fewer shortages: warranty"],"why":"The report is a deliverable, so it is an output. Fewer shortages are a result enabled for stakeholders, so they are an outcome. Producing the report does not guarantee that result.","hook":"Output: what is delivered. Outcome: what changes for someone.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het dagrapport is wat geleverd wordt: output. Minder tekorten is wat managers daarmee bereiken: outcome. Het rapport kan op tijd zijn geleverd zonder dat tekorten dalen. Utility en warranty onderscheiden functionaliteit en afgesproken bruikbaarheid, niet oplevering en effect.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x106","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"A booking service has every required booking function but becomes unavailable during agreed opening hours. Which assessment is best supported?","options":["Its utility is supported, but its warranty is not being met","Its warranty is supported, but its utility is not being met","Its utility and warranty are both demonstrated by the available functions","Its utility is absent because availability is a functional requirement"],"why":"The functionality supports utility. Failure to meet agreed availability undermines warranty. A useful function and dependable delivery are separate considerations.","hook":"Right functions, unreliable delivery: utility without adequate warranty.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De functies ondersteunen de behoefte: utility. Uitval tijdens afgesproken openingstijden schendt warranty. Beschikbaarheid is geen bewijs van de juiste functie en ontbrekende beschikbaarheid betekent niet automatisch dat de functie zelf ontbreekt. Beide aspecten moet je apart beoordelen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x107","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Costs and risks","prompt":"A hosted payroll service removes the need to maintain servers. The customer now pays subscription fees and depends on an external provider. What does this illustrate?","options":["A service can remove some consumer costs and risks while introducing others","A service transfers the customer's accountability for business outcomes to the provider","A service removes costs, while introduced risks are outside the value assessment","A service creates value whenever its fee is lower than the cost of the servers"],"why":"Consumers consider costs and risks removed as well as those introduced. Server savings alone do not establish value, and the customer remains responsible for the outcomes of consumption.","hook":"Check both sides: burdens removed and burdens added.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Serverbeheer kan verdwijnen terwijl abonnementen, training en leveranciersafhankelijkheid erbij komen. Beoordeel kosten en risico's die verdwijnen én ontstaan. De serverbesparing alleen bewijst geen waarde. De customer houdt verantwoordelijkheid voor de outcomes van het gebruik.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x108","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Value","prompt":"Two customers receive the same reports at the same price. One makes faster decisions; the other finds the reports irrelevant. Which explanation best fits ITIL?","options":["Value depends on stakeholder perceptions and the outcomes important to them","Value is the same because both customers receive identical outputs","Value is fixed by the provider when it sets the price of the service","Value is determined by report availability rather than customer use"],"why":"Value depends on perceived benefits, usefulness and importance. Identical outputs or prices can have different value in different stakeholder contexts.","hook":"Same output can mean different value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Waarde hangt af van behoeften en ervaren nut voor stakeholders. Dezelfde output en prijs kunnen daarom verschillende waarde hebben. De provider bepaalt niet eenzijdig de ervaren waarde. Beschikbaarheid helpt, maar bewijst niet dat de klant er iets belangrijks mee bereikt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x109","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service consumption","prompt":"A customer manages employee access to an online learning service and gives the provider feedback. Which service relationship concept includes these activities?","options":["Service consumption","Service provision","Service offering","Service relationship management"],"why":"Consumption includes the consumer's management of resources needed to use a service, use of the service and feedback. Provision describes the provider's activities; an offering describes what is offered.","hook":"Consumption includes managing use and giving feedback.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Dit zijn activiteiten aan de consumentkant: eigen gebruiksmiddelen beheren en feedback leveren hoort bij service consumption. De provider exploiteert de dienst via provision. Een offering beschrijft wat geleverd kan worden; gezamenlijk relatiebeheer benadrukt activiteiten van beide partijen samen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x110","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service offering","prompt":"An offering includes a laptop whose ownership passes to the customer, access to a hosted application, and help with installation. Which classification is correct?","options":["Goods, access to resources, and service actions","Resources, service actions, and goods","Service actions, goods, and access to resources","Access to resources, goods, and service actions"],"why":"The transferred laptop is goods. The hosted application provides access without transferring ownership. Installation assistance is a service action.","hook":"Own it, access it, or have something done.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De laptop wordt eigendom: goods. De applicatie wordt gebruikt zonder eigendomsoverdracht: access to resources. Installatiehulp is verricht werk: service actions. De alternatieven gebruiken dezelfde begrippen maar koppelen ze aan het verkeerde onderdeel.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x201","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using the principles","prompt":"A team uses \"start where you are\" and \"progress iteratively with feedback\" on the same improvement. What explains this?","options":["The principles interact and should be considered together in the situation","Each principle applies to a different mandatory phase of the service lifecycle","One principle must be completed before another becomes applicable","The first principle controls planning and the second is limited to development"],"why":"Guiding principles are broadly applicable and interact. They are not sequential phases or rules assigned to individual practices.","hook":"Principles work together; they are not a sequence.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De principes zijn geen verplichte fasen en niet exclusief voor één practice of type werk. Eerst de huidige situatie begrijpen en vervolgens iteratief verbeteren kan in dezelfde situatie logisch zijn. Principes vullen elkaar aan; je moet hun gezamenlijke relevantie bekijken.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x202","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using the principles","prompt":"Which TWO statements about the guiding principles are correct?\n1. They can guide an organization when its goals or circumstances change.\n2. Each principle belongs to one value chain activity.\n3. They should be considered together rather than in isolation.\n4. An organization must choose one principle to govern all its decisions.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"The principles remain useful across circumstances and complement each other. They are neither allocated one per activity nor mutually exclusive choices.","hook":"Broad guidance, used together.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"1 en 3 zijn juist: principes blijven bruikbaar bij veranderende omstandigheden en horen samen overwogen te worden. 2 verdeelt ze ten onrechte over exclusieve activiteiten. 4 maakt er een keuze tussen onderling uitsluitende regels van. Het zijn samenhangende aanbevelingen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"x203","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Focus on value","prompt":"A team wants to shorten call handling time. Before choosing a target, it asks which results callers need and how the change would affect their experience. Which principle is most directly illustrated?","options":["Focus on value","Start where you are","Optimize and automate","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The decisive action is identifying the results and experience that matter to consumers. Measuring the current state or running iterations could help later, but is not the focus of this description.","hook":"Ask what matters to the person using the service.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het team vraagt welk resultaat en welke ervaring voor de beller belangrijk zijn. Dat is focus on value. Het vertrekpunt observeren zou start where you are benadrukken; feedback per kleine stap iteratie. Kortere gesprekken zijn niet vanzelf meer waarde voor gebruikers.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x204","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Start where you are","prompt":"A proposed redesign assumes the present workflow is unusable. Which action best reflects \"start where you are\"?","options":["Observe the existing work and assess what can usefully be retained","Define the desired future outcome and select measures for it","Divide the replacement into small increments with review points","Remove steps that do not contribute to an agreed outcome"],"why":"Assessing existing work through direct observation identifies useful assets and practices. The other actions can be helpful, but they emphasize value, iteration or simplicity rather than the starting point.","hook":"Look before replacing.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Eerst het echte bestaande werk beoordelen en nuttige onderdelen herkennen hoort bij start where you are. Toekomstdoelen kiezen, kleine stappen maken en overbodig werk verwijderen kunnen daarna nuttig zijn, maar beschrijven niet specifiek het objectief vaststellen van het vertrekpunt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x205","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Progress iteratively with feedback","prompt":"A team delivers a small usable improvement, checks its effects with users, then adjusts the next increment. Which principle is most directly demonstrated?","options":["Progress iteratively with feedback","Collaborate and promote visibility","Think and work holistically","Keep it simple and practical"],"why":"Small increments that are adjusted using feedback are the central clue. User involvement supports collaboration too, but the question emphasizes how work progresses and adapts.","hook":"Small step, feedback, next step.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De beslissende combinatie is kleine bruikbare verbeteringen plus feedback die het volgende stuk werk beïnvloedt. Samenwerking is aanwezig, maar niet de nadruk. Alleen een klein pakket opleveren zonder feedback te gebruiken zou het principe nog niet volledig toepassen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x206","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Collaborate and promote visibility","prompt":"An improvement repeatedly stalls at team boundaries. People with relevant knowledge are brought into decisions, and work status is made visible. Which principle is most directly addressed?","options":["Collaborate and promote visibility","Think and work holistically","Start where you are","Optimize and automate"],"why":"Involving relevant people and making work visible directly address collaboration and visibility. Holistic thinking concerns how the service's parts work together, rather than these particular engagement actions.","hook":"Bring the right people in; make the work visible.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Hier ontbreken deelname van relevante mensen en zichtbaarheid van werk. Dat is collaborate and promote visibility. Holistic thinking kijkt naar het systeem en onderlinge effecten. Die principes kunnen samen helpen, maar mensen betrekken en informatie toegankelijk maken zijn hier specifiek beschreven.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x207","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Think and work holistically","prompt":"The network team reduces its own costs, but the resulting delays increase support costs and damage the overall service. Which principle most directly addresses this local optimization?","options":["Think and work holistically","Progress iteratively with feedback","Start where you are","Keep it simple and practical"],"why":"Holistic thinking considers the entire service and the interactions between its parts. Improving one team's measure can harm the whole.","hook":"Optimize the whole service, not just one team's numbers.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Eén onderdeel scoort beter maar de service als geheel slechter. Holistic thinking vraagt het geheel en de afhankelijkheden te beoordelen. Een lokale besparing is geen succesvolle optimalisatie als die meer schade elders veroorzaakt. Itereren of simpel houden lost die denkfout niet vanzelf op.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x208","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Keep it simple and practical","prompt":"Three approvals were added years ago. A review shows that two no longer contribute to the required outcome or controls. Which action best follows \"keep it simple and practical\"?","options":["Remove the two unnecessary approvals while retaining the useful control","Automate all three approvals so the existing design can run faster","Keep all three approvals but report their completion more visibly","Retain all three until the entire service can be redesigned"],"why":"Simplicity removes work that adds no useful contribution. It does not mean removing necessary controls or automatically preserving and automating every existing step.","hook":"Enough control, no unnecessary work.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Haal stappen weg die geen nuttige bijdrage meer leveren, maar behoud noodzakelijke controle. Dat is keep it simple and practical. Alle bestaande goedkeuringen automatiseren maakt mogelijk onnodig werk alleen sneller. Zichtbaarheid vergroten verklaart ook niet waarom overbodige stappen moeten blijven.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x209","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Optimize and automate","prompt":"A workflow repeatedly sends requests to the wrong team. Which approach best follows \"optimize and automate\"?","options":["Understand and improve the routing, then automate suitable parts","Automate the current routing, then use faster processing as the success measure","Replace human judgment throughout the workflow before reviewing its purpose","Increase the number of automated handoffs while keeping the routing rules"],"why":"Optimization improves the effectiveness and usefulness of the work before suitable automation is applied. Automating faulty routing can repeat the fault faster.","hook":"Fix the flow before speeding it up.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Automatiseer geen foutieve routering zonder eerst de werking te begrijpen en verbeteren. Meer snelheid herhaalt dan vooral de fout sneller. Optimize and automate combineert nuttig verbeteren met passende technologie; het eist niet dat elk menselijk oordeel verdwijnt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x210","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Start where you are","prompt":"A dashboard suggests that requests take ten minutes, but users describe long waits. Which response best reflects \"start where you are\"?","options":["Observe actual request handling and compare it with what the dashboard measures","Adopt the dashboard result as the baseline because it is quantitative","Replace the request process using a design from another organization","Set a faster target first and use that target to judge the existing process"],"why":"Measurements can be incomplete or misleading. Direct observation helps establish the actual starting point and the meaning of the reported measures.","hook":"Check what a measure really measures.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een dashboard kan een ander deel van de wachttijd meten dan gebruikers ervaren. Direct observeren en controleren wat cijfers betekenen helpt het echte vertrekpunt vaststellen. Getallen zijn niet automatisch volledig of juist en een toekomsttarget is nog geen nulmeting.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x211","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Focus on value","prompt":"A technically successful release is rarely used. Which question most directly follows \"focus on value\"?","options":["Does the release help its intended consumers achieve something important to them?","Were the existing infrastructure components reused where possible?","Was the release divided into sufficiently small deployment batches?","Can the deployment workflow be completed with fewer manual steps?"],"why":"Technical completion alone does not establish value. The focus is the benefit for the intended consumers. Reuse, small batches and automation address different considerations.","hook":"Delivered is not the same as valuable.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een technische release kan slagen zonder belangrijk klantresultaat. Focus on value vraagt naar het nut voor de bedoelde gebruikers. Hergebruik, kleine batches en minder handwerk wijzen op andere principes. Zij bewijzen op zichzelf niet dat de nieuwe functie waarde heeft.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x212","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Progress iteratively with feedback","prompt":"A team splits a project into small releases but reviews the results only after the final release. Which element of \"progress iteratively with feedback\" is missing?","options":["Using feedback during the work to influence subsequent increments","Preparing a detailed plan for every increment before starting the first","Giving every increment the same duration and resource allocation","Completing each increment without depending on other service activities"],"why":"Small pieces alone are insufficient. Feedback should inform decisions while there is still an opportunity to adjust the work.","hook":"A small batch needs a learning loop.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Werk in kleine stukken knippen is maar een deel van het principe. Feedback moet tijdig volgende beslissingen beïnvloeden. Alles vooraf vastleggen, identieke blokgroottes of alle afhankelijkheden wegdenken is niet de ontbrekende kern. Het gaat om leren terwijl bijsturen nog kan.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x301","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Organizations and people","prompt":"A service has suitable tools and suppliers, but staff lack the skills and decision authority needed to use them. Which dimension is most directly involved?","options":["Organizations and people","Information and technology","Partners and suppliers","Value streams and processes"],"why":"Skills, responsibilities and authority belong primarily to organizations and people. All four dimensions interact, but the stated weakness is about people and organizational arrangements.","hook":"Skills and authority: organizations and people.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Vaardigheden, verantwoordelijkheden en bevoegdheden horen bij organizations and people. Goede tools en leveranciers leveren die niet automatisch. De werkvolgorde hoort eerder bij value streams and processes; de zin richt zich op mensen en organisatie-inrichting.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x302","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Information and technology","prompt":"A team checks whether knowledge is accurate, accessible and protected, and whether its systems can exchange data. Which dimension is most directly addressed?","options":["Information and technology","Organizations and people","Partners and suppliers","Value streams and processes"],"why":"Information quality, protection and technology integration fall within information and technology. This dimension includes the information itself, not just hardware and software.","hook":"The information matters as much as the tools.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De informatie zelf telt mee bij information and technology: juistheid, toegang, bescherming en uitwisseling. De dimensie is breder dan apparatuur. De vraag gaat niet primair over vaardigheden, leveranciersrelaties of de volgorde van werk, ook al hangen die ermee samen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x303","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Partners and suppliers","prompt":"An organization decides which capabilities to keep internally and which to obtain through external agreements. Which dimension most directly covers this decision?","options":["Partners and suppliers","Organizations and people","Information and technology","Value streams and processes"],"why":"Sourcing strategy and relationships with other organizations belong primarily to partners and suppliers. Internal skills influence the decision, but the question focuses on sourcing.","hook":"Who provides what, through which relationship?","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Zelf doen of via externe afspraken inkopen is een sourcingkeuze binnen partners and suppliers. Interne vaardigheden kunnen de afweging beïnvloeden, maar vormen niet het centrale onderwerp. Onderscheid het aandachtspunt van andere factoren die ook meespelen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x304","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Value streams and processes","prompt":"Departments each work efficiently, yet requests wait between them. A review maps the sequence of work and its handoffs from demand to delivery. Which dimension is most directly involved?","options":["Value streams and processes","Organizations and people","Partners and suppliers","Information and technology"],"why":"This dimension concerns how activities, workflows, controls and procedures combine to create value. Mapping the flow across departments exposes delays that local measures miss.","hook":"Follow the work from need to result.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het in kaart brengen van werk van aanvraag tot levering hoort bij value streams and processes. Goed presterende afdelingen kunnen samen een trage service vormen door wachttijd bij overdrachten. Alleen teamvaardigheden of techniek beoordelen is dan te beperkt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x401","criterion":"4.1","lo":4,"tag":"Service value system","prompt":"Which set contains only components of the ITIL service value system?","options":["Governance, practices, continual improvement","Plan, Engage, Deliver and support","Organizations and people, partners and suppliers, governance","Demand, opportunity, value"],"why":"Governance, practices and continual improvement are SVS components, alongside the guiding principles and service value chain. The other sets name chain activities, mix dimensions with a component, or name inputs and an outcome.","hook":"SVS components include principles, governance, chain, practices and improvement.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Governance, practices en continual improvement zijn SVS-componenten. Samen met guiding principles en de service value chain vormen zij het systeem. Plan, Engage en Deliver and support zijn ketenactiviteiten; dimensions zijn perspectieven; demand en opportunity zijn input en value het beoogde resultaat.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x402","criterion":"4.1","lo":4,"tag":"Service value system","prompt":"Which statement best describes the purpose of the service value system?","options":["It shows how organizational components and activities work together to enable value creation","It specifies one sequence that every service request must follow to completion","It assigns each practice to exactly one activity in a service delivery lifecycle","It describes only the provider's technical resources used to deliver services"],"why":"The SVS connects organizational components and activities in the creation of value. It is broader than technical resources and does not impose a single sequence or one-to-one practice assignment.","hook":"The system connects the organization's work to value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het SVS beschrijft hoe organisatorische onderdelen en activiteiten samenwerken voor waarde. Niet alleen techniek, geen verplichte éénrichtingsprocedure en geen één-op-één-koppeling tussen practice en activiteit. Het geheel is breder dan de route van één verzoek.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x501","criterion":"5.1","lo":5,"tag":"Value streams","prompt":"A value stream uses Engage, then Design and transition, then returns to Engage for clarification. How should this be understood?","options":["Activities can be revisited and combined as needed within a value stream","The return to Engage means a new service value system must be created","Each activity must be completed once before any earlier activity is revisited","A valid value stream must follow the displayed value chain order without loops"],"why":"Value chain activities are interconnected. A value stream combines them in a suitable flow, including revisiting activities where useful; the chain is not a fixed waterfall sequence.","hook":"A value chain is flexible; a value stream follows the actual need.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een value stream mag activiteiten herhalen of anders combineren als dat bij het werk past. De value chain is geen vaste watervalvolgorde. Teruggaan naar Engage voor verduidelijking maakt de stroom niet ongeldig en vereist geen nieuw SVS.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x502","criterion":"5.1","lo":5,"tag":"Value streams","prompt":"Which TWO statements about the value chain and practices are correct?\n1. Each practice is assigned exclusively to one value chain activity.\n2. Different value streams can combine value chain activities differently.\n3. Every value stream must contain the same sequence of activities.\n4. A practice can contribute to more than one value chain activity.","options":["2 and 4","1 and 2","1 and 3","3 and 4"],"why":"Practices provide capabilities that can support several activities. Value streams combine activities for particular needs, so neither exclusive assignments nor an identical sequence is required.","hook":"Many practices can support many activities.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"2 en 4 zijn juist: verschillende waardestromen gebruiken activiteiten anders en dezelfde practice kan meerdere activiteiten ondersteunen. 1 maakt de koppeling ten onrechte exclusief. 3 schrijft ten onrechte overal dezelfde volgorde voor. Middelen en werkstromen zijn flexibel te combineren.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"x503","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Plan","prompt":"Which value chain activity establishes a shared understanding of the vision, current status and improvement direction across the organization?","options":["Plan","Improve","Engage","Design and transition"],"why":"Plan establishes the shared understanding of direction and the current position. Improve concerns ongoing improvement across products, services, practices and the value chain.","hook":"Plan: shared direction and shared understanding.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Plan zorgt voor gedeeld begrip van visie, huidige status en verbeterrichting. Het woord improvement maakt dit niet automatisch Improve. Improve ondersteunt doorlopende verbetering over producten, services, practices en activiteiten; Engage richt zich op stakeholders.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x504","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Improve","prompt":"Which value chain activity ensures ongoing improvement across products, services and practices, and across the value chain itself?","options":["Improve","Plan","Obtain/build","Deliver and support"],"why":"Improve explicitly covers continual improvement at these different levels. Plan aligns understanding and direction, while the other activities focus on components or delivery.","hook":"Improve reaches across the chain.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Improve richt zich expliciet op verbetering over services, practices, producten, ketenactiviteiten en dimensies. Plan schept gedeelde richting. Obtain/build verzorgt componenten en Deliver and support operationele levering. Kijk naar de reikwijdte van het doel.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x505","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Engage","prompt":"The purpose includes understanding stakeholder needs, maintaining transparency and sustaining good stakeholder relationships. Which value chain activity is this?","options":["Engage","Plan","Design and transition","Deliver and support"],"why":"These stakeholder-facing objectives define Engage. Relationships may matter throughout the chain, but this is the activity whose purpose centers on that engagement.","hook":"Engage: needs, transparency and relationships.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Behoeften begrijpen, transparantie en stakeholderrelaties zijn de kern van Engage. Design and transition zorgt vervolgens dat producten en services aan verwachtingen voldoen. Relaties zijn overal nuttig, maar juist dit specifieke doel hoort bij Engage.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x506","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Design and transition","prompt":"Which value chain activity ensures that products and services meet stakeholder expectations for quality, costs and time to market?","options":["Design and transition","Obtain/build","Deliver and support","Engage"],"why":"Design and transition addresses those expectations for new or changed products and services. Obtain/build concerns having suitable components available; Deliver and support concerns agreed delivery and support.","hook":"Design and transition: ready to meet expectations.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Kwaliteit, kosten en time to market van nieuwe of gewijzigde producten en services wijzen op Design and transition. Obtain/build gaat over componenten volgens specificatie. Deliver and support gaat over dagelijkse levering; Engage over behoeften en relaties begrijpen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x507","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Obtain/build","prompt":"A team ensures that service components are available when needed and meet the agreed specifications. Which value chain activity best matches this purpose?","options":["Obtain/build","Design and transition","Deliver and support","Plan"],"why":"Obtain/build focuses on the availability and specifications of service components. Designing the overall service and supporting it in operation have different purposes.","hook":"Obtain/build: the right components, available when needed.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De beschikbaarheid van componenten volgens specificatie is Obtain/build, ongeacht of die intern gebouwd of extern gekocht worden. De totale dienst ontwerpen is een ander doel. Een operationele service volgens afspraken leveren valt onder Deliver and support.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x508","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Deliver and support","prompt":"Which value chain activity ensures that services are delivered and supported according to agreed specifications and stakeholder expectations?","options":["Deliver and support","Design and transition","Obtain/build","Engage"],"why":"This is the purpose of Deliver and support. The wording concerns ongoing delivery and support rather than developing the service or obtaining its components.","hook":"Deliver and support: make the agreed service work for people.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Operationele levering en ondersteuning volgens afgesproken specificaties is Deliver and support. Vergelijk met componenten verkrijgen, producten ontwerpen en behoeften begrijpen. Overeenkomende woorden zoals specificatie maken die doelen niet identiek.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x601","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Information security management","prompt":"Which practice protects the information an organization needs for its business, including its confidentiality, integrity and availability?","options":["Information security management","Service configuration management","IT asset management","Monitoring and event management"],"why":"Information security management protects business information. Configuration management provides information about configurations, asset management concerns asset lifecycles and value, and monitoring observes state changes.","hook":"Protect information: security. Describe components: configuration.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Informatie beschermen is information security management. Configuration management zorgt voor configuratie- en afhankelijkheidsinformatie. Asset management kijkt naar financiële waarde en levenscyclus. Monitoring observeert relevante toestandsveranderingen. Het specifieke beschermingsdoel beslist.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x602","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Relationship management","prompt":"Which practice establishes and nurtures links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels?","options":["Relationship management","Service desk","Supplier management","Service level management"],"why":"Relationship management develops stakeholder relationships broadly. The service desk is a contact point for users, supplier management focuses on suppliers and service level management agrees business-based service targets.","hook":"Stakeholder relationships beyond individual tickets.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Strategische en tactische stakeholderrelaties vormen de brede focus van relationship management. Supplier management focust specifiek op leveranciers. Service level management bepaalt servicetargets; service desk is de gebruikersingang. Allemaal contacten, maar met verschillende doelen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x603","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Supplier management","prompt":"Which practice ensures that suppliers and their performance are managed appropriately to support quality products and services?","options":["Supplier management","Relationship management","Service level management","IT asset management"],"why":"Supplier management focuses specifically on suppliers and their performance. Relationship management has broader stakeholder scope; service level management focuses on service quality targets and assessment.","hook":"Supplier performance is the key clue.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Leveranciers en hun prestaties beheren hoort bij supplier management. Relationship management is breder. Service level management spreekt af wat de service voor de business moet leveren. Asset management beheert waarde en levenscyclus van assets, niet primair leveranciersprestaties.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x604","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset management","prompt":"Which practice plans and manages the full lifecycle of IT assets to help control costs and risks and maximize value?","options":["IT asset management","Service configuration management","Deployment management","Supplier management"],"why":"Asset management addresses the lifecycle and value of financially valuable IT assets. Configuration management focuses on reliable information about service configurations and their relationships.","hook":"Asset: lifecycle, cost, risk and value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Waarde, kosten, risico en volledige levenscyclus van IT-assets is IT asset management. Service configuration management levert betrouwbare configuratie- en relatie-informatie. Deployment verplaatst componenten. Eén component kan bij verschillende practices relevant zijn; de nadruk verschilt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x605","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Monitoring and event management","prompt":"Which practice systematically observes services and components and records selected changes of state as events?","options":["Monitoring and event management","Incident management","Problem management","Service configuration management"],"why":"Monitoring and event management observes and handles relevant state changes. An event can be informational; incident management addresses disruption or degraded service rather than every event.","hook":"Notice the state change before deciding what it means.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Observeren, registreren en verwerken van geselecteerde relevante toestandsveranderingen is monitoring and event management. Een event is niet per definitie een verstoring. Incident management richt zich op herstel; problem management op oorzaken; configuration management op informatie over de inrichting.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x606","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Release management","prompt":"Which practice makes new or changed services and features available for use?","options":["Release management","Deployment management","Change enablement","Service configuration management"],"why":"Release management concerns availability for use. Deployment moves components into environments, while change enablement assesses risk and authorization. Installed software may not yet be released to users.","hook":"Release: available to use. Deployment: moved into place.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Beschikbaar maken voor gebruik is release management. Deployment verplaatst componenten naar een omgeving; die kunnen nog achter een uitgeschakelde feature flag staan. Change enablement beoordeelt risico en autoriseert. Deze activiteiten kunnen apart in de tijd plaatsvinden.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x607","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service configuration management","prompt":"Which practice ensures that accurate information about service configurations, supporting items and their relationships is available when needed?","options":["Service configuration management","IT asset management","Monitoring and event management","Service level management"],"why":"Configuration management supplies trustworthy configuration information and relationships. Asset management has a financial lifecycle focus, while monitoring tracks state changes.","hook":"Configuration: what supports what?","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Betrouwbare informatie over configuraties en hun onderlinge relaties is service configuration management. IT asset management benadrukt financiële waarde en levenscyclus. Monitoring registreert events. Alleen een inventarislijst met prijzen is niet voldoende om serviceafhankelijkheden te begrijpen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x608","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Deployment management","prompt":"Which practice moves new or changed hardware, software, documentation or other components into live environments, and may also move them into test environments?","options":["Deployment management","Release management","Change enablement","IT asset management"],"why":"Deployment moves components between environments. Release makes features available for use, and change enablement assesses and authorizes changes. These purposes are related but distinct.","hook":"Deployment moves; release makes available.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Verplaatsen van nieuwe of gewijzigde componenten naar omgevingen is deployment management. Release maakt ze beschikbaar voor gebruik. Change enablement beoordeelt en autoriseert wijzigingen. Het installeren zelf is dus niet hetzelfde als toestemming of beschikbaarstelling voor gebruikers.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x609","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"Which practice aligns services and working methods with changing business needs through ongoing improvements?","options":["Continual improvement","Service level management","Change enablement","Problem management"],"why":"Continual improvement has the broad purpose of ongoing alignment and improvement. Service level management sets and assesses service targets; change enablement controls changes; problem management addresses incident causes.","hook":"Keep services and working methods aligned as needs change.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Continual improvement houdt services en practices blijvend passend bij veranderende businessbehoeften. Het is breder dan incidentoorzaken onderzoeken of individuele changes autoriseren. Service level management bepaalt en bewaakt servicekwaliteitstargets; die kunnen verbeteringen helpen aanwijzen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x610","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Change enablement","prompt":"Which practice aims to increase successful product and service changes through risk assessment, authorization and schedule management?","options":["Change enablement","Release management","Deployment management","Continual improvement"],"why":"Those three responsibilities identify change enablement. Release and deployment concern making functionality available and moving components; improvement has a broader ongoing alignment purpose.","hook":"Assess, authorize and coordinate changes.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Risico beoordelen, changes autoriseren en de change schedule beheren vormen change enablement. Release maakt iets bruikbaar voor gebruikers; deployment verplaatst onderdelen. Continual improvement omvat de bredere blijvende verbetering. Eén traject kan al deze practices toepassen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x611","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Incident management","prompt":"Which purpose belongs to incident management?","options":["Reduce the impact of incidents by restoring normal service promptly","Reduce future incidents by identifying causes and managing workarounds","Observe services and record selected changes of state","Handle agreed user requests through predefined workflows"],"why":"Incident management prioritizes restoring service. Finding actual or potential causes is problem management; observing state changes is monitoring; agreed normal requests belong to service request management.","hook":"Incident management: restore service.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Incident management beperkt negatieve gevolgen via zo snel mogelijk normaal serviceherstel. Oorzaken en workarounds beheren hoort bij problem management, events observeren bij monitoring en normale aanvragen afhandelen bij request management. Herstel hoeft niet te wachten op een permanente fix.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x612","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Problem management","prompt":"Which practice reduces the likelihood and impact of incidents by identifying causes and managing workarounds and known errors?","options":["Problem management","Incident management","Monitoring and event management","Change enablement"],"why":"Problem management addresses actual and potential causes and the management of workarounds and known errors. Incident management focuses on restoring service following disruption.","hook":"Problem management: understand causes and reduce their effects.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Problem management vermindert kans en impact via oorzakenonderzoek en het beheren van workarounds en known errors. Incident management focust op actueel serviceherstel. Monitoring kan signalen leveren, maar neemt het oorzakenonderzoek niet automatisch over.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x613","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service request management","prompt":"Which practice handles predefined, user-initiated requests as part of normal service delivery in an effective, user-friendly way?","options":["Service request management","Service desk","Incident management","Change enablement"],"why":"Service request management handles agreed normal requests through suitable workflows. The desk may receive those requests, but its purpose as a contact point is different from fulfilling them.","hook":"Receive at the desk; fulfil through request management.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Vooraf gedefinieerde normale gebruikersverzoeken effectief afhandelen is service request management. De desk kan ze ontvangen, maar ontvangst is niet de hele afhandeling. Incident management herstelt verstoringen; change enablement regelt risico en autorisatie van wijzigingen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x614","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service desk","prompt":"Which practice captures demand for incident resolution and service requests and provides a contact point between provider and users?","options":["Service desk","Service request management","Incident management","Relationship management"],"why":"Capturing this demand and providing the user contact point are central to the service desk. Incident and request management address the work that follows; relationship management has broader stakeholder scope.","hook":"Service desk: the user's contact point.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het centrale contactpunt en het opvangen van incident- en requestvraag zijn de service desk. De afhandeling kan andere teams en practices gebruiken. Relationship management gaat over bredere strategische en tactische stakeholderrelaties, niet specifiek deze gebruikersingang.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x615","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Which practice sets clear, business-based service targets and ensures delivery is assessed and managed against them?","options":["Service level management","Relationship management","Supplier management","Monitoring and event management"],"why":"Service level management connects agreed service quality to business needs and assesses performance. Monitoring provides observations, but does not replace agreement on meaningful service targets.","hook":"Agree what good service means, then assess it.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Service level management stelt businessgerichte servicekwaliteitstargets vast en beoordeelt de daadwerkelijke levering daartegen. Monitoring levert waarnemingen, maar bepaalt niet vanzelf wat een goed target is. Supplier management gaat over leveranciers; relationship management over bredere relaties.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x616","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Known error and problem","prompt":"Complete the statement: a problem that has been analysed but has not yet been resolved is a [?].","options":["Known error","Incident","Event","Change"],"why":"An analysed, unresolved problem is a known error. A workaround is useful where available, but is not required by this definition. An incident is a disruption or reduction in service quality.","hook":"Known error: analysed and still unresolved.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Known error betekent een geanalyseerd maar nog niet opgelost problem. Een workaround is geen voorwaarde in die definitie. Een incident is de verstoring zelf; een event de relevante toestandsverandering; een change een toevoeging, wijziging of verwijdering met mogelijk service-effect.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"missing-word"},{"id":"x617","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset and configuration item","prompt":"Which pairing correctly distinguishes an IT asset from a configuration item (CI)?","options":["IT asset: financially valuable component; CI: component managed to deliver a service","IT asset: component managed to deliver a service; CI: financially valuable component","IT asset: component in production; CI: component in a test environment","IT asset: physical component; CI: logical component"],"why":"An IT asset has financial value and contributes to IT service delivery. A CI is a component that needs management to deliver a service. The same component may satisfy both descriptions; neither category is limited to physical or logical items.","hook":"Asset and CI are different views that can overlap.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"IT asset benadrukt financiële waarde; CI benadrukt dat iets beheerd moet worden voor servicelevering. Een onderdeel kan beide zijn. Het onderscheid is niet hardware versus software of productie versus test. Kijk naar het criterium, niet naar de fysieke vorm.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x618","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event and incident","prompt":"Which description defines an event?","options":["A state change that is significant for managing a service or configuration item","An unplanned service interruption or reduction in service quality","An actual or potential cause of one or more incidents","An addition, modification or removal that may affect services"],"why":"An event is a significant change of state. The other choices describe an incident, a problem and a change. An event does not necessarily indicate service failure.","hook":"Event means significant state change, not automatically failure.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een event is een beheersmatig relevante toestandsverandering. De andere beschrijvingen betreffen incident, problem en change. Een event kan informeren zonder dat een service verslechtert. Een melding alleen bewijst dus geen incident of geanalyseerde oorzaak.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x619","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Change","prompt":"Which description defines a change?","options":["An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly","Movement of a new or modified component into a live environment","A new or modified service or feature becoming available for use","An unexpected interruption or reduction in the quality of a service"],"why":"A change includes additions, modifications and removals with possible service effects. Deployment and release are more specific concepts; an incident is disruption or degraded quality.","hook":"Change includes indirect effects and removals too.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een change is breder dan deployment of release: toevoegen, wijzigen of verwijderen van iets dat direct of indirect services kan beïnvloeden. Een incident is ongeplande verstoring of kwaliteitsvermindering. De wijziging hoeft nog niet in productie te staan om een change te zijn.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x701","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: vision","prompt":"An improvement team knows the current waiting time. Before selecting a target, it confirms how shorter waits support the organization's objectives. Which model step does that confirmation belong to?","options":["What is the vision?","Where are we now?","Where do we want to be?","How do we get there?"],"why":"Connecting the improvement to organizational direction belongs to the vision step, even if some baseline data already exists. A numeric future target belongs to \"Where do we want to be?\".","hook":"Vision: why this improvement matters to the organization.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De handeling verbindt de verbetering aan organisatiedoelen: What is the vision? Dat er al meetgegevens liggen verandert het doel van deze specifieke stap niet. Een meetbaar toekomsttarget is Where do we want to be?; concrete acties kiezen is How do we get there?","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x702","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: baseline","prompt":"A team documents the existing workflow, assesses available skills and measures current performance. Which continual improvement model step is this?","options":["Where are we now?","What is the vision?","Where do we want to be?","Did we get there?"],"why":"These activities assess the current state and establish a baseline. \"Did we get there?\" evaluates achieved results against the target after action has been taken.","hook":"Baseline first; achieved results later.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De bestaande situatie en mogelijkheden beoordelen is Where are we now? Het is een nulmeting. Did we get there? gebruikt ook cijfers, maar pas om na uitvoering resultaten met het doel te vergelijken. Het moment en het meetdoel zijn beslissend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x703","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: target","prompt":"The current fulfilment time is five days. The team agrees that success means two days by the end of the quarter. Which step does agreeing this target represent?","options":["Where do we want to be?","What is the vision?","How do we get there?","Did we get there?"],"why":"A specific desired future state belongs to \"Where do we want to be?\". The improvement plan explains how to reach it; evaluating results checks whether it was reached.","hook":"The target is the destination, not the route.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Twee dagen aan het einde van het kwartaal is het gewenste meetbare eindpunt. Daarom Where do we want to be? Het vertelt nog niet hoe je daar komt. Het woord deadline maakt een target geen uitvoeringsplan; achteraf resultaat meten is weer een andere stap.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x704","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: plan","prompt":"The vision, baseline and measurable target have been agreed. The team chooses actions, resources and an order for carrying them out. Which step is it performing?","options":["How do we get there?","Where do we want to be?","Take action","How do we keep the momentum going?"],"why":"Choosing the route and arranging the work creates the improvement plan. Executing that plan is \"Take action\". Maintaining gains belongs to the momentum step.","hook":"Planning the work is different from doing the work.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Acties, middelen en volgorde kiezen beschrijft de route: How do we get there? Uitvoeren is Take action. Het target is al vastgesteld. Resultaat vasthouden hoort bij momentum en volgt op een bereikt en geëvalueerd resultaat.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x705","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: action","prompt":"An agreed improvement plan calls for a revised workflow. Staff now put the workflow into use and carry out the planned changes. Which model step is this?","options":["Take action","How do we get there?","Where do we want to be?","Did we get there?"],"why":"Implementing the plan is \"Take action\". Planning the changes and evaluating their achieved effects are separate steps, even though feedback can be used throughout.","hook":"The plan is now being carried out.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De afgesproken wijzigingen worden daadwerkelijk uitgevoerd: Take action. Ze bedenken en plannen is How do we get there? Beoordelen of het resultaat bereikt is, is Did we get there? Feedback kan overal helpen, maar die doelen blijven verschillend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x706","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: evaluation","prompt":"After an improvement, the team compares measured results with the agreed target and determines whether the objective was achieved. Which step is this?","options":["Did we get there?","Where are we now?","Where do we want to be?","How do we keep the momentum going?"],"why":"Comparing achieved results with the intended target evaluates success. Measuring the initial baseline is \"Where are we now?\"; sustaining the result addresses momentum.","hook":"Compare the result with the destination you chose.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De gerealiseerde resultaten vergelijken met het afgesproken doel is Did we get there? De oorspronkelijke nulmeting is Where are we now? De gewenste toekomstige situatie vaststellen is Where do we want to be?; resultaat borgen is momentum.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x707","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: momentum","prompt":"The target has been reached. A manager reinforces the new behavior, communicates the benefits and helps the team avoid returning to old methods. Which step is most directly illustrated?","options":["How do we keep the momentum going?","Did we get there?","Take action","What is the vision?"],"why":"These actions sustain and build on achieved improvements. Evaluating whether the target was reached has already happened; preserving the gains is the current emphasis.","hook":"Keep the gains from slipping away.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het doel is al behaald. Nieuwe gewoonten ondersteunen en terugval voorkomen hoort bij How do we keep the momentum going? Nogmaals vaststellen of het target behaald is zou evaluatie zijn. De beschreven nadruk is behoud en verder bouwen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x708","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"Which TWO statements about continual improvement are correct?\n1. Everyone should have responsibility for contributing to improvement.\n2. A dedicated improvement team takes all improvement responsibility away from other staff.\n3. Entering an idea in a register means it has been approved for implementation.\n4. Improvement ideas can be recorded and prioritized in a continual improvement register.","options":["1 and 4","1 and 2","2 and 3","3 and 4"],"why":"Everyone can contribute, with dedicated people providing support and coordination. A register helps manage opportunities; recording an idea is not the same as authorizing or implementing it.","hook":"Capture ideas, assess them, and keep responsibility shared.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"1 en 4 zijn juist. Iedereen kan bijdragen en een register ondersteunt vastleggen en prioriteren van kansen. Een apart team haalt verantwoordelijkheid niet weg bij de rest. Een idee registreren is geen toestemming om het direct uit te voeren.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"x709","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident management","prompt":"A workaround restores a failed service to normal operation. The cause is still unknown. Which statement best describes the situation?","options":["The incident can be resolved after restoration is confirmed, while cause investigation continues separately","The incident must remain unresolved until the underlying problem is permanently removed","The unknown cause means the workaround cannot count as service restoration","The incident becomes a service request once a workaround is available"],"why":"Incident management focuses on confirmed service restoration and can resolve an incident without removing its underlying cause. Problem management can continue investigating; appropriate confirmation and closure procedures still apply.","hook":"Restore the service; investigate the cause through problem management.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Na bevestigd serviceherstel kan het incident opgelost worden volgens de geldende procedure. Problem management kan de oorzaak verder onderzoeken. Een workaround bewijst geen definitieve oplossing, maar het ontbreken van root cause blokkeert niet automatisch incidentherstel.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x710","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident prioritization","prompt":"Incident A affects a payroll deadline due in one hour. Incident B has more reports but affects a non-critical feature with an agreed workaround. What should guide their priority?","options":["Business impact and urgency, using the agreed prioritization approach","The total number of reports, because that establishes the resolution order","The order in which the first report for each incident was received","The estimated technical effort, with the quickest restoration attempted first"],"why":"Priority should reflect business impact and urgency. Report count, arrival order and repair effort can provide context but do not by themselves establish business priority.","hook":"Priority asks how much it matters and how soon action is needed.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Impact op de business en urgentie bepalen prioriteit volgens afspraken. Meer meldingen betekent niet automatisch hogere prioriteit. Aankomstvolgorde of technische oplostijd kan context geven, maar mag de gevolgen van een kritieke deadline niet vervangen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x711","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident management","prompt":"A service desk cannot restore an incident using its available knowledge. Which response best supports incident management?","options":["Involve suitable specialists while maintaining coordination and communication","Retain ownership within the first team until it identifies the cause","Resolve the incident record when a specialist accepts the handover","Delay restoration while a separate team completes cause analysis"],"why":"Incident management can draw on different teams and suppliers to restore service. Escalating to expertise does not remove the need for coordination or keeping users informed.","hook":"Bring in expertise without losing coordination.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Gebruik passende expertise en houd herstel en communicatie gecoördineerd. Het incident hoeft niet bij het eerste team te blijven tot de oorzaak bekend is. Alleen overdragen of anders classificeren is geen serviceherstel. Gebruikers blijven tijdige informatie nodig hebben.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x712","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Problem management","prompt":"Trend analysis identifies a component likely to cause future service interruptions, although it has not yet caused one. How does this relate to problem management?","options":["Problem management can investigate a potential cause before an incident occurs","A problem can be recorded only after the first associated incident is resolved","The potential cause is already a known error because it has been detected","The potential cause should be treated as an incident regardless of service impact"],"why":"Problems include potential causes of incidents, so identification can be proactive. Detection alone does not establish an analysed known error, and a potential future interruption is not itself an incident.","hook":"Problem management can act before the first disruption.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een problem kan een potentiële oorzaak zijn, dus onderzoek mag vóór het eerste incident plaatsvinden. Alleen een risico of defect opmerken is nog geen analyse voor known error. Zonder actuele serviceverstoring is het evenmin automatisch een incident.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x713","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Known errors and workarounds","prompt":"A problem has been analysed and remains unresolved. No effective workaround has been found. Which statement is correct?","options":["It can still be a known error; a workaround is not a prerequisite for that definition","It becomes a known error only when a workaround is documented","It remains an incident until an effective workaround restores service","It must be recorded as a change because the analysis is complete"],"why":"The known error definition requires an analysed, unresolved problem. A workaround may reduce its effects, but its absence does not stop the problem from being a known error.","hook":"Analysed and unresolved is enough for a known error.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Analyse plus nog onopgelost maakt dit een known error. Een effectieve workaround is geen voorwaarde. Het blijft niet uitsluitend een incident tot iemand een omweg heeft. Een change kan later nodig zijn voor de oplossing, maar is niet hetzelfde als het problem.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x714","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Problem management","prompt":"A permanent fix would cost much more than the expected benefit. An effective workaround keeps the remaining impact acceptable. Which approach best fits problem management?","options":["Assess and manage the residual risk, keeping the known error and workaround under review","Treat the problem as permanently resolved because the workaround is effective","Require a permanent fix before any related incidents can be resolved","Stop reviewing the known error once its workaround has been documented"],"why":"Problem management balances costs, risks and benefits; not every problem receives an immediate permanent fix. An accepted workaround does not remove the need to manage the unresolved issue.","hook":"Managed risk may be preferable to an unjustified fix.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Afwegen van kosten, risico en baten kan betekenen dat een permanente fix wordt uitgesteld. Blijf het resterende risico en de workaround beheren. Een effectieve omweg maakt de oorzaak niet permanent opgelost en is geen reden om alle beoordeling te stoppen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x715","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Standard changes","prompt":"A low-risk installation follows a well-understood, fully documented and pre-authorized procedure. Which statement is correct?","options":["It can be a standard change when carried out within the authorized conditions","It is a normal change because each execution needs a new authorization","It is an emergency change because a separate approval step is unnecessary","It is outside change enablement because the installation is routine"],"why":"A standard change is low risk, well understood, documented and pre-authorized. The authorization applies to the defined procedure and conditions, not to arbitrary variations.","hook":"Standard means pre-authorized within a defined scope.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Standard change geldt binnen de bekende, gedocumenteerde en vooraf geautoriseerde voorwaarden. Routine betekent niet buiten change enablement. Voor een afwijkende uitvoering kan nieuwe autorisatie nodig zijn. Spoed en geen losse goedkeuringsstap zijn niet hetzelfde.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x716","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Emergency changes","prompt":"An urgent security patch is needed to address a serious vulnerability. What is appropriate for an emergency change?","options":["Use an accelerated assessment and authorization path appropriate to the urgency","Use the standard change path because urgent work is automatically pre-authorized","Deploy first in every case, then obtain retrospective authorization as the normal rule","Use the normal lead time even when the delay would leave unacceptable exposure"],"why":"Emergency changes need expedited handling, with assessment and authorization adapted to urgency. Emergency status does not itself mean pre-authorization or the absence of controls.","hook":"Urgency changes the speed and path, not the need for control.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een emergency change krijgt passende versnelde beoordeling en autorisatie. Urgentie betekent niet automatisch vooraf geautoriseerd, ongecontroleerd uitvoeren of altijd achteraf goedkeuren. De normale doorlooptijd blind vasthouden kan de resterende blootstelling vergroten.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x717","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change authority","prompt":"Two changes have different risks and potential impacts. How should their change authorities be selected?","options":["Use the appropriate authority for each type and level of risk","Send every change to the same senior committee to ensure consistency","Give the implementing technician authority for every change they perform","Use the same authority whenever changes are scheduled for the same day"],"why":"An appropriate authority should be assigned to the type of change and its risk. This can be an individual or group; a single committee need not authorize every change.","hook":"Match the authority to the change.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De change authority hoort te passen bij type en risico. Dat kan een persoon of groep zijn. Eén commissie hoeft niet alles te autoriseren; een uitvoerder is ook niet automatisch voor iedere eigen wijziging bevoegd. De kalenderdatum bepaalt het risico niet.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x718","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change schedule","prompt":"Two independently approved changes affect the same service during the same maintenance window. What is the main value of the change schedule here?","options":["Making the overlap visible so the changes can be coordinated and conflicts managed","Providing authorization that replaces the approvals already given for the changes","Showing that each change has met all technical acceptance criteria","Converting both changes into standard changes because their timing is known"],"why":"A change schedule helps coordinate work, communicate plans and identify conflicts. Being on the schedule does not replace authorization or prove successful testing.","hook":"A schedule coordinates; it does not authorize by itself.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De change schedule toont planning, mogelijke botsingen en afhankelijkheden. Afstemmen blijft nodig wanneer wijzigingen afzonderlijk al zijn goedgekeurd. Een kalenderitem geeft geen extra autorisatie, bewijst geen geslaagde tests en maakt een change niet standaard.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x719","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request management","prompt":"A user requests access under an agreed request model, but the model requires a manager's approval. Which handling is appropriate?","options":["Follow the predefined request workflow, including the required approval","Treat it as an incident because access has not yet been granted","Skip the approval because all service requests are pre-authorized changes","Start a problem investigation because the user cannot currently perform the activity"],"why":"Service requests are agreed normal service actions, but their workflows can still include approvals and security checks. A request is not automatically an incident or a pre-authorized change.","hook":"Normal request does not mean no approval.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een vooraf afgesproken request kan gewoon een goedkeuringsstap bevatten. Volg het model. Nog geen nieuw recht hebben is niet automatisch een incident. Routineverzoeken zijn niet allemaal pre-authorized changes en een mogelijke vertraging is niet vanzelf een problem.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x720","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request management","prompt":"A user asks for an agreed standard software installation. The request workflow includes a pre-authorized change. Which statement is most accurate?","options":["Request management handles fulfilment, while the change follows its authorized change model","The request must be reclassified as an incident because installation changes the service","Request management replaces change enablement whenever a user initiates the work","The standard change must become a normal change each time a user requests it"],"why":"Practices can work together. A service request can include a standard change without losing its request workflow or bypassing the conditions of pre-authorization.","hook":"One request can draw on more than one practice.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een service request kan een standard change bevatten. Request management coördineert de afhandeling en het change-model blijft gelden. De practices vervangen elkaar niet. Het verzoek maakt de change niet automatisch normal of het ticket een incident.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x721","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk","prompt":"Routine requests increasingly use self-service. Which capability becomes particularly valuable for the service desk's remaining interactions?","options":["Understanding users and business context, with effective communication and empathy","Measuring success mainly by reducing the duration of every conversation","Taking over every specialist team's technical resolution responsibilities","Requiring users to identify the correct technical team before making contact"],"why":"Automation can leave more complex or sensitive interactions for people. Communication, empathy and business understanding remain essential; the desk need not personally solve every specialist issue.","hook":"Automation increases the importance of the human interaction.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Door automatisering blijven vaak complexere menselijke contacten over. Begrip van de gebruiker, empathie en communicatie blijven daarom belangrijk. De desk hoeft niet elke specialistische oplossing zelf te leveren. Gespreksduur verkorten is geen doel los van goede hulp.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x722","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk","prompt":"A service desk operates from several locations but should act as one coherent contact point. Which arrangement best supports this?","options":["Shared information and tools, with coordinated ways of working and communication","Independent local records, with users responsible for carrying information between desks","A rule that incidents can be handled only at the location where they were reported","Optimize each local queue without coordinating the overall user experience"],"why":"A virtual or distributed desk can provide coherent support through shared tools, information and working practices. Physical co-location is not the defining requirement.","hook":"One experience can come from several locations.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een verdeelde desk kan één contactpunt vormen met gedeelde informatie, tools en gecoördineerde werkwijzen. Fysiek bij elkaar zitten is niet vereist. Gebruikers telkens opnieuw informatie laten overdragen of cases aan één locatie vastzetten maakt de ondersteuning minder samenhangend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x723","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Individual infrastructure targets are met, but customers cannot complete transactions quickly enough. Which response best supports service level management?","options":["Review end-to-end service targets and actual customer experience","Report success because the component targets have all been achieved","Average the component scores to obtain the customer's service experience","Replace customer feedback with more detailed measurements of each component"],"why":"Service targets should reflect business outcomes and the overall experience. Good component results can coexist with poor end-to-end service, so component metrics alone are insufficient.","hook":"Green components can still add up to a poor service.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Groene infrastructuurtargets bewijzen geen goede end-to-end service. Bekijk het echte businessresultaat, de gebruikerservaring en de gekozen targets. Meer componentmetingen of succes rapporteren op basis van losse onderdelen lost de slechte transactieservice niet op.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x724","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Which TWO inputs together provide a useful basis for understanding service performance?\n1. The provider's assumptions without checking with consumers.\n2. Customer and user discussions about their experience.\n3. Measured service results.\n4. Component availability treated as a complete substitute for service experience.","options":["2 and 3","1 and 2","3 and 4","1 and 4"],"why":"Quantitative measures and qualitative discussions complement each other. Assumptions and isolated component metrics cannot fully establish whether the service meets consumer needs.","hook":"Combine numbers with conversations.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"2 en 3 zijn juist: gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers en gemeten serviceresultaten vullen elkaar aan. Provider-aannames zonder controle zijn onvoldoende. Losse componentbeschikbaarheid is geen volledige vervanging voor de echte service-ervaring.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"x725","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"A provider and customer are drafting an SLA. Which approach best supports meaningful service level management?","options":["Agree clear service targets that relate to business needs and can be understood by both parties","List every internal technical measure and treat that list as the service commitment","Base commitments on what is easiest to measure before discussing customer outcomes","Let each technical team define its own commitments without checking the overall service"],"why":"SLAs should express agreed service expectations in a clear, business-relevant way. Internal technical detail can support delivery, but is not a substitute for meaningful service commitments.","hook":"An SLA should describe service quality that the customer can recognize.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een SLA bevat duidelijke, gezamenlijk begrijpelijke targets die bij businessbehoeften passen. Niet alles wat intern meetbaar is, is een zinvolle servicebelofte. Bespreek eerst relevante outcomes; laat lokale teamtargets niet het beeld van de hele service vervangen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-001","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"A reporting service meets its agreed availability target but cannot produce the forecast its customer requires. Which assessment is supported?","options":["Warranty is supported, but the required utility is missing","Utility is supported, but the required warranty is missing","Both utility and warranty are demonstrated by availability","Neither utility nor warranty can be assessed from these facts"],"why":"Availability supports warranty; the missing required function concerns utility. Meeting one does not establish the other.","whyNl":"De afgesproken beschikbaarheid wordt gehaald: dat ondersteunt warranty. De vereiste forecastfunctie ontbreekt: utility ontbreekt voor die behoefte. Niet alles is dus onvoldoende, maar beschikbaarheid bewijst ook niet dat de dienst de juiste functie heeft.","hook":"Separate required functionality from agreed conditions of use.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-002","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"A service can perform the required calculations. It also maintains agreed response times under the expected load. Which pairing is correct?","options":["Required calculation: utility; assured performance under load: warranty","Required calculation: warranty; assured performance under load: utility","Required calculation: output; assured performance under load: outcome","Required calculation: outcome; assured performance under load: output"],"why":"The capability addresses the need; assurance about capacity and performance supports use. Outputs and outcomes concern deliverables and resulting effects, not this distinction.","whyNl":"De berekenmogelijkheid is functionaliteit, dus utility. Afgesproken prestaties onder belasting gaan over bruikbaarheid en capaciteit, dus warranty. Een gegenereerd rapport zou output zijn; een betere beslissing dankzij het rapport een outcome.","hook":"Can do the task; can be relied on under agreed conditions.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-003","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Consumer roles","prompt":"A manager defines the service requirements, approves its budget and uses it. Which conclusion is correct?","options":["The manager performs customer, sponsor and user roles","The manager is a sponsor, so cannot also be a customer","The manager is a customer, while the provider performs the user role","The manager performs one consumer role determined by seniority"],"why":"Roles describe responsibilities and actions; one person can perform several. Seniority does not make the roles mutually exclusive.","whyNl":"Eisen bepalen wijst op customer, budget autoriseren op sponsor en gebruiken op user. De rollen zijn geen exclusieve functietitels. Eén persoon kan alle drie uitvoeren en de provider wordt daardoor niet de gebruiker namens de klant.","hook":"Classify the action, not the job title.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-004","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service and offering","prompt":"A description presents a hosted payroll service to a target group, including access and support actions. What is that formal description?","options":["A service offering","A service","A product","A service relationship"],"why":"The question asks about the description of the proposed services, not the arrangement enabling outcomes, the underlying resource configuration or the cooperation itself.","whyNl":"Een formele beschrijving voor een doelgroep is een service offering. De service helpt outcomes te bereiken. Een product is een configuratie van middelen; een service relationship is de samenwerking tussen provider en consument. Kijk naar wat precies benoemd wordt: de beschrijving.","hook":"Offering describes what is offered.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-005","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service management","prompt":"Which distinction between a practice and service management is correct?","options":["A practice arranges resources for work or an objective; service management concerns capabilities enabling customer value through services","A practice defines service consumption outcomes; service management authorizes the consumer's budget","A practice is the sequence of value chain activities; service management is one activity in that sequence","A practice describes what a customer can buy; service management is the delivery of that description"],"why":"Practices are resource sets supporting work. Service management is the broader capability for enabling value through services; neither is a consumer role or a sales description.","whyNl":"Een practice bundelt organisatorische middelen om werk te doen of een doel te bereiken. Service management is breder: capaciteiten voor waarde via services. De andere opties verwisselen dit met klantrollen, de waardeketen of een service offering.","hook":"Resources for a purpose versus broader service-management capability.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-006","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Outputs and outcomes","prompt":"A team delivers an accurate stock report on time, but managers do not use it and shortages remain unchanged. What has been demonstrated?","options":["An output has been delivered; the desired outcome has not been demonstrated","The desired outcome has been delivered because the report is accurate","No output has been delivered because shortages remain unchanged","The output and outcome are the same because both belong to one service"],"why":"The report is a deliverable, whether or not it produces the intended result. Fewer shortages would be a stakeholder result enabled by using it.","whyNl":"Het rapport is output, ook als niemand er iets mee doet. Minder tekorten zou de gewenste outcome zijn. Op tijd en nauwkeurig opleveren bewijst niet dat dat resultaat is bereikt; het uitblijven van resultaat wist de oplevering niet uit.","hook":"Delivery is not proof of the desired result.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-007","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Costs and risks","prompt":"A managed service removes server-maintenance work, but the consumer must train staff and manage supplier dependency. Which value assessment is appropriate?","options":["Consider both costs and risks removed and those introduced by consumption","Compare the service fee with server cost and omit remaining consumer work","Assess introduced risks separately from whether the service offers value","Assume the provider now owns responsibility for the consumer's business outcomes"],"why":"A value assessment includes benefits, costs and risks on both sides of the change. Removing server work does not remove every consumer responsibility.","whyNl":"Beoordeel wat verdwijnt én wat erbij komt. Training kost geld of middelen en leveranciersafhankelijkheid kan risico introduceren. Alleen de factuur met serverkosten vergelijken is te beperkt. De customer blijft verantwoordelijk voor outcomes van het servicegebruik.","hook":"Removed and introduced both matter.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-008","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Value co-creation","prompt":"A provider meets the technical specification, but customers explain that a different result matters to them. What best supports value co-creation?","options":["Work with the customers to understand the needed outcomes and adapt the service relationship","Treat the agreed technical output as sufficient evidence of equal value for every customer","Transfer responsibility for discovering needs entirely to customers after delivery","Use the provider's delivery cost as the measure of customer value"],"why":"Value is co-created through cooperation and depends on what stakeholders need and perceive, not merely on delivered specifications or provider cost.","whyNl":"Technisch opleveren is niet hetzelfde als waarde voor een klant. Provider en consument moeten samen de relevante outcomes begrijpen. De kostprijs van de provider bepaalt geen klantwaarde en verantwoordelijkheid volledig bij de klant leggen is geen gezamenlijke waardecreatie.","hook":"Co-create value rather than declare it delivered.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-009","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"Which TWO statements are correct?\n1. A function can meet a need while its availability remains inadequate.\n2. Meeting availability targets proves the service has the required functions.\n3. Both functionality and agreed conditions of use matter when assessing value.\n4. Utility and warranty are alternative names for the same property.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"A service can have useful functions but inadequate assurance. Functionality and dependable use are distinct and both contribute to value.","whyNl":"1 is juist: een functie kan nuttig zijn maar te vaak onbeschikbaar. 3 is juist: beide aspecten tellen. 2 verwisselt beschikbaarheid met functionaliteit; 4 maakt twee verschillende begrippen ten onrechte gelijk.","hook":"Useful is not automatically dependable.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"contrast-010","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service offering","prompt":"A provider retains ownership of a server but lets a customer use its computing capacity. Which offering component is this?","options":["Access to resources","Goods","Service actions","Transfer of service ownership"],"why":"Access lets the consumer use a resource while the provider retains ownership. Goods involve ownership transfer; service actions are performed activities.","whyNl":"De klant gebruikt capaciteit zonder eigenaar te worden: access to resources. Goods vereist eigendomsoverdracht. Service actions betreft uitgevoerd werk. De toegang draagt niet automatisch eigendom van de service over.","hook":"Use without ownership transfer.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-011","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service relationship activities","prompt":"The provider maintains its platform. The consumer trains its own users. Together they review cooperation. Which order correctly identifies these activities?","options":["Service provision; service consumption; service relationship management","Service consumption; service provision; service relationship management","Service provision; service relationship management; service consumption","Service relationship management; service consumption; service provision"],"why":"Provider-side delivery, consumer-side use and joint management of the relationship are distinct but connected activities.","whyNl":"Het platform onderhouden is providerwerk: provision. Eigen gebruikers voorbereiden is consumentwerk: consumption. Samen de samenwerking beheren is relationship management. Niet elke activiteit waarbij een provider betrokken is, is automatisch gezamenlijk relatiebeheer.","hook":"Provider work; consumer work; joint relationship work.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-012","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Consumer responsibilities","prompt":"A customer buys a managed collaboration service. Which activity is still an example of service consumption?","options":["Managing the customer's own resources needed to use the service","Operating the provider's platform as part of the agreed hosting service","Publishing the provider's formal description of the offering","Managing the provider's resources required to supply the service"],"why":"Consumption includes the consumer's resources and actions required for use. The other activities are on the provider or offering side of the relationship.","whyNl":"De consument houdt eigen activiteiten, zoals medewerkers en gebruiksrechten beheren. Het platform en providermiddelen exploiteren zijn provision. Een formele propositie publiceren gaat over de offering. Managed betekent dus niet dat de klant niets meer hoeft te doen.","hook":"Consumption still includes the consumer's work.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-013","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"A principle remains useful after an organization changes its strategy. What best explains this?","options":["Guiding principles are recommendations intended to guide many circumstances","Guiding principles apply only while the original strategy remains approved","Each strategy selects one principle and suspends the remaining principles","Principles prescribe the same detailed procedure for every strategy"],"why":"Principles offer broadly applicable guidance, rather than strategy-specific procedures or mutually exclusive rules.","whyNl":"Guiding principles bieden brede aanbevelingen. Een strategiewijziging maakt ze niet automatisch ongeldig. De organisatie kiest niet één principe dat de andere uitschakelt en de principes schrijven ook geen universele detailprocedure voor.","hook":"General guidance, adapted to the circumstances.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-014","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"A team improves a service by considering user value, observing existing work and using feedback. How should its use of principles be understood?","options":["Several principles complement one another in the same situation","Only the first principle used applies to the decision","Each principle must be assigned to a different team","Using several principles turns them into value chain activities"],"why":"Principles interact and support one another. They are not exclusive selections or organizational assignments.","whyNl":"Verschillende principes ondersteunen dezelfde beslissing. Waarde begrijpen, de huidige situatie beoordelen en feedback gebruiken kunnen samen. Dat maakt principes geen fasen, teams of value-chainactiviteiten.","hook":"Consider principles together.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-015","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which TWO statements describe guiding principles correctly?\n1. They may help with decisions in any practice.\n2. They specify a compulsory lifecycle order.\n3. Their relevance should be considered together in context.\n4. They replace the need to understand stakeholder needs.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Principles are broadly applicable and should be considered as a connected set. They do not replace understanding the situation or impose a lifecycle sequence.","whyNl":"1 en 3 zijn juist. Principes geven richting binnen uiteenlopende practices en werken samen. 2 verwart ze met verplichte fasen; 4 negeert juist het begrijpen van stakeholders, wat essentieel blijft.","hook":"Recommendations, not lifecycle phases.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"contrast-016","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Focus on value","prompt":"A team can add a requested feature cheaply, but first asks whether it will help users complete the task that matters to them. Which principle is emphasized?","options":["Focus on value","Keep it simple and practical","Start where you are","Optimize and automate"],"why":"The decision is anchored in the consumer's useful result. Low cost is background, not evidence that the team is simplifying or automating work.","whyNl":"De doorslag geeft wat gebruikers bereiken. Dat de feature goedkoop is, maakt dit geen keep it simple of optimize and automate. De huidige situatie objectief bekijken zou start where you are zijn; hier staat gebruikerswaarde voorop.","hook":"What useful result will this create?","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-017","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Start where you are","prompt":"An existing service has a poor reputation. Before replacing it, the team checks direct observations rather than assuming every part is unusable. Which principle is emphasized?","options":["Start where you are","Focus on value","Think and work holistically","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The team establishes the actual starting point and what is useful. It has not yet divided implementation into feedback-driven increments.","whyNl":"Het team beoordeelt de werkelijke bestaande situatie. Slechte reputatie bewijst niet dat alles weg moet. Holistisch kijken betreft het gehele systeem; iteratief werken vraagt kleine uitvoeringsstappen met feedback. Die zijn hier nog niet beschreven.","hook":"Assess before discarding.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-018","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Iteration and collaboration","prompt":"All teams share a dashboard, but they plan to wait until the whole programme is complete before reviewing effects. Which principle would most directly improve how the work progresses?","options":["Progress iteratively with feedback","Collaborate and promote visibility","Start where you are","Keep it simple and practical"],"why":"Visibility is already present. What is missing is timely feedback that changes subsequent increments of work.","whyNl":"De gedeelde informatie ondersteunt al visibility. Het probleem is wachten met feedback tot alles af is. Kleine stappen met tijdige feedback verbeteren juist het verloop van het werk. Simpel houden of een nulmeting lost dat gemis niet specifiek op.","hook":"Visible work still needs timely feedback.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-019","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Collaboration and holistic thinking","prompt":"A team already understands the end-to-end service, but relevant specialists cannot access the decisions or contribute their knowledge. Which principle is most directly missing?","options":["Collaborate and promote visibility","Think and work holistically","Optimize and automate","Start where you are"],"why":"The stated gap is participation and information access, not knowledge of the overall system.","whyNl":"Het geheel is al in beeld. Het ontbreekt aan mensen betrekken en informatie zichtbaar maken: collaborate and promote visibility. Holistic thinking is dus niet de beste keuze voor precies dit beschreven tekort.","hook":"Understanding the whole is not the same as involving people.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-020","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Holistic thinking","prompt":"A team proposes a change that improves its response target but transfers extra work to another team and slows the customer journey. Which principle most directly challenges the proposal?","options":["Think and work holistically","Collaborate and promote visibility","Keep it simple and practical","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The proposal optimizes a part at the expense of the whole. Communication and iteration may help, but the decisive assessment is end-to-end value.","whyNl":"De lokale score verbetert terwijl de hele service slechter wordt. Dat vraagt holistic thinking. Samenwerken en itereren kunnen helpen, maar de kern van de fout is optimaliseren van één deel ten koste van het geheel.","hook":"Optimize the service, not just one team's metric.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-021","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Simplicity and automation","prompt":"A workflow contains duplicate information entry. The team removes the duplicate step while keeping the needed check. No technology change is involved. Which principle is most directly illustrated?","options":["Keep it simple and practical","Optimize and automate","Collaborate and promote visibility","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The action removes unnecessary complexity without discarding a useful control. There is no described use of automation.","whyNl":"Onnodig werk wordt weggehaald en noodzakelijke controle blijft. Dat is keep it simple and practical. Verbeteren kan ook bij optimize horen, maar de expliciete nadruk hier is eenvoud zonder een automatiseringsstap.","hook":"Remove waste without removing necessary controls.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-022","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Optimize and automate","prompt":"A team wants software to fulfil routine requests. What is the best first step under optimize and automate?","options":["Understand and improve the work before automating suitable steps","Automate the current workflow before deciding what outcomes matter","Remove every human decision to maximize the number of automated steps","Select the fastest tool before assessing the existing work"],"why":"Automation should support an understood, useful and optimized workflow. Tool speed and automation count are not substitutes for effectiveness.","whyNl":"Eerst begrijpen welk werk nuttig is en hoe het beter kan. Daarna automatiseer je geschikte stappen. Een tool kiezen op snelheid, fouten sneller uitvoeren of alle menselijke oordelen uitsluiten is niet het doel.","hook":"Improve the work, then automate what suits it.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-023","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Using feedback","prompt":"A team receives feedback after each small release but never uses it to change later work. Which action best completes the principle being attempted?","options":["Use relevant feedback to reassess and adjust subsequent increments","Collect additional feedback only after the final release","Give each increment a fixed size regardless of what is learned","Replace user feedback with a count of completed releases"],"why":"Feedback must inform decisions, not simply be collected. The size of releases or amount of feedback does not by itself show learning.","whyNl":"Feedback verzamelen is niet hetzelfde als ermee bijsturen. Pas volgende stappen aan op basis van relevante bevindingen. Meer formulieren, vaste blokgroottes of releases tellen bewijzen geen leren.","hook":"Feedback has to influence the next decision.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-024","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Measurement and direct observation","prompt":"Which action should be avoided when applying start where you are?","options":["Treating existing measurements as a substitute for observing actual work","Checking what existing resources remain useful","Comparing measured performance with user experience","Assessing the current situation before selecting a replacement"],"why":"Measures may omit important aspects or distort behaviour. They should support observation rather than replace it.","whyNl":"Vermijd blind vertrouwen op cijfers zonder het echte werk te bekijken. Metingen zijn nuttig, maar kunnen iets anders meten dan wat gebruikers ervaren. De andere opties ondersteunen juist een betrouwbare beoordeling van het vertrekpunt.","hook":"Measurements support observation; they do not replace it.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"negative"},{"id":"contrast-025","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Four dimensions","prompt":"An organization introduces a tool and agrees supplier support, but nobody understands the new responsibilities. Which dimension is the clearest gap?","options":["Organizations and people","Information and technology","Partners and suppliers","Value streams and processes"],"why":"Responsibilities and understanding concern people and the organization. A working tool and supplier contract do not supply that capability.","whyNl":"Het tekort betreft begrip en verantwoordelijkheden: organizations and people. De aanwezigheid van een tool of contract lost dat niet op. Een probleem in de volgorde van werk zou eerder value streams and processes benadrukken.","hook":"Tools and contracts do not replace role clarity.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-026","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Four dimensions","prompt":"Which statement about the four dimensions is correct?","options":["They need balanced consideration because they interact across services and the SVS","Each dimension corresponds to one exclusive stage of the value chain","A strong technology dimension compensates automatically for the other dimensions","Only the dimensions directly controlled by the provider need consideration"],"why":"The dimensions are connected perspectives used across service management, including dependencies the provider does not directly control.","whyNl":"De dimensies hangen samen en gelden over de gehele service. Het zijn geen afzonderlijke ketenfasen. Goede techniek compenseert geen ontbrekende vaardigheden en externe afhankelijkheden moet je ook meenemen.","hook":"Four perspectives on the same service.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-027","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Information and technology","prompt":"A review asks whether service knowledge can be trusted, found by the right people and exchanged between systems. Which dimension is most directly addressed?","options":["Information and technology","Value streams and processes","Organizations and people","Partners and suppliers"],"why":"The subject is information quality, accessibility and integration. The mention of people using it does not make staff capability the main issue.","whyNl":"Het onderwerp is de informatie en de technologie om die te delen. Dat mensen toegang nodig hebben, verandert de hoofdzaak niet in vaardigheden of cultuur. Een werkvolgorde of leveranciersafspraak staat niet centraal.","hook":"The information itself is part of this dimension.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-028","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Value streams and processes","prompt":"A service's tools and staff are adequate, but work spends most of its time waiting between activities. Which review most directly addresses the relevant dimension?","options":["Trace the end-to-end workflow, handoffs and controls","Assess staff roles, skills and organizational culture","Assess data structures and application interoperability","Review external sourcing arrangements and contracts"],"why":"Waiting across handoffs is primarily about how work is integrated into a value stream. The other reviews address the remaining dimensions.","whyNl":"De wachttijd zit tussen activiteiten: onderzoek de waardestroom, overdrachten en controles. Rollen en cultuur horen bij people; data en systemen bij information and technology; sourcing bij partners. Allemaal nuttig, maar niet even direct voor dit probleem.","hook":"Follow the flow, not only the individual teams.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-029","criterion":"3.1","lo":3,"tag":"Partners and suppliers","prompt":"A provider compares retaining a capability internally with using a specialized external organization. Which concern most directly belongs to partners and suppliers?","options":["The sourcing strategy and arrangements for working with the external organization","The competency and authority of each internal employee","The format and protection of service information","The detailed order of activities within a fulfilment workflow"],"why":"Sourcing and relationships with other organizations define the main concern; the remaining options focus on the other dimensions.","whyNl":"De beslissing gaat over sourcing en samenwerking met een externe partij. Interne competenties beïnvloeden de keuze, maar vormen de people-dimensie. Datavormen en de detailwerkstroom zijn andere perspectieven.","hook":"Sourcing and external relationships.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-030","criterion":"4.1","lo":4,"tag":"Service value system","prompt":"Which pairing correctly identifies the main inputs and the intended result of the service value system?","options":["Opportunity and demand are inputs; value is the intended result","Value and demand are inputs; governance is the intended result","Practices and value are inputs; opportunity is the intended result","Governance and opportunity are inputs; demand is the intended result"],"why":"Opportunity and demand prompt the organization's response. Its connected components enable value; governance and practices are components rather than the main inputs or result.","whyNl":"Opportunity en demand vormen input. Het SVS laat zien hoe samenwerkende onderdelen waarde mogelijk maken. Governance en practices zijn componenten van het systeem, niet de bedoelde uitkomst. De alternatieven verwisselen deze categorieën.","hook":"Opportunity and demand in; value enabled.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-031","criterion":"4.1","lo":4,"tag":"Service value system","prompt":"How does the service value chain relate to the service value system?","options":["It is one component within the broader system","It is an alternative name for the entire system","It contains the four dimensions as consecutive steps","It replaces practices once a value stream is selected"],"why":"The value chain is an SVS component alongside governance, principles, practices and continual improvement. It does not replace these or turn dimensions into phases.","whyNl":"De value chain is één onderdeel van het SVS. Het hele systeem omvat daarnaast governance, guiding principles, practices en continual improvement. De vier dimensies zijn perspectieven, geen opeenvolgende stappen binnen de keten.","hook":"The chain is inside the system.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-032","criterion":"4.1","lo":4,"tag":"Service value system","prompt":"Which TWO statements are correct?\n1. Governance is a component of the SVS.\n2. The SVS is restricted to technical operations.\n3. Practices can support the activities through which value is created.\n4. The SVS prescribes one fixed flow for all demand.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"The system includes governance and the practices supporting value creation. It is broader than technical operations and does not require a single fixed flow.","whyNl":"1 en 3 zijn juist. Governance stuurt en beheerst; practices leveren middelen voor werk. 2 maakt het systeem te beperkt en 4 behandelt een flexibel samenwerkend systeem als één verplichte procedure.","hook":"A connected system, not a universal procedure.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"contrast-033","criterion":"4.1","lo":4,"tag":"Governance and practices","prompt":"Which description most specifically identifies governance rather than a practice or the value chain?","options":["How an organization is directed and controlled","Resources arranged for performing particular work","Interconnected activities combined into value streams","Recurring improvement to meet stakeholder expectations"],"why":"Direction and control identify governance. Resource sets are practices, interconnected activities the value chain, and recurring improvement another SVS component.","whyNl":"Sturen en beheersen is governance. Middelen voor een doel zijn practices. Verbonden activiteiten vormen de value chain. Doorlopend verbeteren is continual improvement. Alle opties horen bij hetzelfde systeem, maar hebben een verschillend doel.","hook":"Governance = direction and control.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-034","criterion":"5.1","lo":5,"tag":"Value streams and the chain","prompt":"A provider uses the same value chain activities in different sequences for restoring a service and introducing a new one. What does this demonstrate?","options":["Different value streams combine activities to suit different needs","Each activity has changed into a different practice","The provider must define a separate SVS for every sequence","The second sequence is invalid unless it matches the first"],"why":"Value streams arrange value chain activities in flows suited to particular demand or opportunity. There is no single mandatory sequence for all work.","whyNl":"Verschillende doelen vragen verschillende waardestromen. De activiteiten hoeven geen vaste volgorde te volgen en veranderen daardoor niet in practices. Ook is niet voor iedere route een nieuw SVS nodig.","hook":"Same activities; different flows.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-035","criterion":"5.1","lo":5,"tag":"Practices and activities","prompt":"A practice supports both Engage and Deliver and support. Which conclusion is correct?","options":["Practices can contribute resources to several value chain activities","A practice must be divided because each belongs to one activity","The two activities must be merged because they use one practice","The practice becomes a value stream when used twice"],"why":"Practices provide organizational resources and can support multiple activities. Sharing a practice does not erase the distinction between activities.","whyNl":"Een practice levert middelen voor werk en kan meerdere activiteiten ondersteunen. Je hoeft de practice of activiteiten daarom niet te splitsen of samen te voegen. Twee keer gebruiken maakt een practice evenmin een waardestroom.","hook":"Practices are not assigned one-to-one to activities.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-036","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Plan and Improve","prompt":"A provider aligns teams on the current position, overall vision and direction for improvement. Which value chain activity has this purpose?","options":["Plan","Improve","Engage","Design and transition"],"why":"Plan creates shared understanding of vision, status and direction. Improve ensures improvement across products, services, practices and activities; agreement on direction is not the same purpose.","whyNl":"Plan zorgt voor gezamenlijk begrip van visie, huidige situatie en richting. Improve gaat over voortdurend verbeteren over de hele keten. Het woord improvement in de vraag maakt Improve dus niet automatisch juist.","hook":"Direction and shared understanding point to Plan.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-037","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Improve and Plan","prompt":"A team ensures that working practices and services are continually improved across the whole value chain. Which activity's purpose is most directly represented?","options":["Improve","Plan","Design and transition","Obtain/build"],"why":"Improve explicitly spans ongoing improvement of services, practices and value chain activities. Plan is shared direction; the other choices address design and components.","whyNl":"De brede doorlopende verbetering is Improve. Plan schept richting, Design and transition borgt verwachtingen bij producten en services, Obtain/build zorgt voor geschikte componenten. Het gaat niet alleen om een plan maken.","hook":"Improve spans the chain and dimensions.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-038","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Engage and Design and transition","prompt":"Which purpose distinguishes Engage from Design and transition?","options":["Understanding stakeholder needs and maintaining transparent ongoing relationships","Ensuring changed services meet expectations for quality, cost and time to market","Making service components available according to their specifications","Delivering operational services according to agreed specifications"],"why":"Engage emphasizes understanding, transparency and relationships. The other purposes identify Design and transition, Obtain/build, and Deliver and support respectively.","whyNl":"Engage begrijpt behoeften en onderhoudt transparante relaties. Design and transition laat producten en services aan kwaliteits-, kosten- en doorlooptijdverwachtingen voldoen. Componenten verzorgen is Obtain/build; operationeel leveren is Deliver and support.","hook":"Understand needs versus design to meet expectations.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-039","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Design and transition","prompt":"A team checks that a changed service will meet stakeholder expectations for quality, cost and time to market. Which activity is the closest match?","options":["Design and transition","Obtain/build","Deliver and support","Engage"],"why":"The focus is on expectations for the service as designed and transitioned, rather than component supply, ongoing operation or relationship understanding.","whyNl":"Het gaat om verwachtingen voor het gewijzigde product of de service als geheel. Obtain/build focust op componenten volgens specificatie. Deliver and support betreft operationele levering. Engage begrijpt de behoeften, maar heeft niet hetzelfde doel.","hook":"Expectations for the changed service as a whole.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-040","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Obtain/build and delivery","prompt":"A required database component is purchased and made available when needed, meeting its specification. Which value chain activity best fits this purpose?","options":["Obtain/build","Deliver and support","Design and transition","Improve"],"why":"Obtain/build covers service components obtained externally as well as those built internally. Purchase does not make it ordinary operational delivery.","whyNl":"Obtain/build omvat kopen én bouwen. De component moet beschikbaar zijn waar en wanneer nodig en aan de specificatie voldoen. Operationele servicelevering is Deliver and support; dat is niet hetzelfde als componenten beschikbaar maken.","hook":"Obtain includes buying, not just coding.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-041","criterion":"5.2","lo":5,"tag":"Deliver and support","prompt":"Which purpose belongs to Deliver and support rather than Obtain/build?","options":["Ensuring ongoing service delivery and support meet agreed specifications","Ensuring required service components are available to agreed specifications","Ensuring a common view of vision and improvement direction","Ensuring stakeholder needs and relationships are understood"],"why":"Deliver and support concerns the delivered service. Obtain/build focuses on components, Plan on shared direction, and Engage on stakeholders.","whyNl":"Beide eerste opties noemen specificaties, maar het object verschilt: de operationele service versus benodigde componenten. Servicelevering en ondersteuning is Deliver and support. Richting is Plan, behoeften en relaties is Engage.","hook":"Check whether the question concerns components or the running service.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-042","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Release and deployment","prompt":"Code is installed in production behind a disabled feature flag. A later action makes the feature available to users. Which pairing best fits the purposes?","options":["Installation: deployment management; availability for use: release management","Installation: release management; availability for use: deployment management","Installation: change enablement; availability for use: configuration management","Installation: configuration management; availability for use: change enablement"],"why":"Deployment moves components to an environment; release makes services or features available for use. Authorization and configuration information have other purposes.","whyNl":"Installeren is deployment, beschikbaar maken voor gebruik is release. Ze kunnen op verschillende momenten plaatsvinden. Change enablement beoordeelt risico en autoriseert; configuration management zorgt voor betrouwbare informatie over de configuratie.","hook":"Moved into an environment is not yet available for use.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-043","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Assets and configurations","prompt":"Which objective most directly belongs to service configuration management?","options":["Making reliable configuration and relationship information available when needed","Managing financial value and lifecycle costs of all IT assets","Making changed features available for use by their intended users","Moving new components into the required operational environment"],"why":"Configuration management provides accurate configuration and relationship information. Financial lifecycle, release availability and physical movement are distinct purposes.","whyNl":"Configuratie-informatie en relaties tussen onderdelen zijn doorslaggevend. Financiële levenscyclus wijst op IT asset management. Beschikbaar maken voor gebruik is release; verplaatsen naar een omgeving is deployment.","hook":"Configurations and relationships, not only financial inventory.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-044","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Incident and problem management","prompt":"A team focuses on reducing recurring failures by identifying causes and managing known errors. Which practice's purpose does this match?","options":["Problem management","Incident management","Monitoring and event management","Service request management"],"why":"Reducing likelihood and impact through cause investigation, workarounds and known errors is problem management. Restoration is incident management; observation and routine fulfilment differ.","whyNl":"Oorzaken en known errors beheren om herhaling en impact te verminderen is problem management. Incident management herstelt de actuele service. Monitoring observeert; request management handelt afgesproken normale verzoeken af.","hook":"Causes and recurrence versus immediate restoration.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-045","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Requests and the desk","prompt":"Which purpose most clearly distinguishes service request management from the service desk?","options":["Effective, user-friendly handling of predefined user-initiated requests","Capturing demand and providing a single contact point for users","Reducing incident impact through rapid service restoration","Setting and assessing business-based service targets"],"why":"Request management is responsible for handling agreed requests; the desk captures demand and communicates with users. The remaining purposes are incident and service level management.","whyNl":"Request management verzorgt effectieve afhandeling van vooraf afgesproken gebruikersverzoeken. De desk is de ingang en het contactpunt. Herstel is incident management; servicetargets bepalen en bewaken is service level management.","hook":"Receiving a request is not the whole fulfilment practice.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-046","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Relationship and supplier management","prompt":"Which purpose is specific to supplier management?","options":["Managing suppliers and their performance to support quality service provision","Nurturing strategic and tactical links with all stakeholders","Agreeing business-based targets for the service delivered to customers","Capturing users' demand for incident resolution and service requests"],"why":"Supplier management focuses on suppliers and their performance. The other options describe relationship management, service level management and the desk.","whyNl":"Leveranciers en hun prestaties zijn specifiek supplier management. Relationship management betreft stakeholders breder. Service level management gaat over servicekwaliteitstargets; de service desk over de gebruikersingang.","hook":"Supplier performance is a specific relationship concern.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-047","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Information security","prompt":"Protecting the confidentiality, integrity and availability of business information is the purpose of which practice?","options":["Information security management","Service configuration management","Monitoring and event management","IT asset management"],"why":"Information security protects information needed by the organization. Configuration accuracy, observing events and managing asset value are related but different goals.","whyNl":"Informatie beschermen is information security management. Betrouwbare configuratiegegevens leveren is configuration management. Monitoring constateert gebeurtenissen. Asset management beheert financiële waarde en levenscyclus. Het object informatie maakt niet alle practices gelijk.","hook":"Protection of information is the central purpose.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-048","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Monitoring and incidents","prompt":"A practice systematically observes service components and selects state changes to record and report. Which practice is described?","options":["Monitoring and event management","Incident management","Problem management","Service level management"],"why":"Observation and handling selected state changes define monitoring and event management. Events can inform other practices without all being incidents.","whyNl":"Observeren en relevante toestandsveranderingen registreren hoort bij monitoring and event management. Een event kan informatief zijn. Herstel, oorzakenonderzoek en servicetargets beoordelen zijn andere doelen, ook als zij monitoringgegevens gebruiken.","hook":"An observation is not automatically a service failure.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-049","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Change enablement","prompt":"Which set of activities best matches the purpose of change enablement?","options":["Assess risks, authorize changes and manage the change schedule","Move components, install packages and switch production environments","Make features available for use and communicate their availability","Maintain component information and map service dependencies"],"why":"Risk assessment, authorization and scheduling help maximize successful changes. The alternatives emphasize deployment, release and configuration purposes.","whyNl":"Het doel wordt ondersteund door risico beoordelen, autoriseren en de change schedule beheren. Installeren is deployment, voor gebruik vrijgeven is release en afhankelijkheidsinformatie bijhouden is configuration management. Eén wijziging kan al deze practices nodig hebben.","hook":"Risk, authorization and schedule.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-050","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"Which purpose belongs to continual improvement rather than change enablement?","options":["Ongoing alignment of practices and services with changing business needs","Authorization and coordination of individual product and service changes","Restoration of normal service following an interruption","Management of information describing service configurations"],"why":"Continual improvement continuously aligns and improves the organization. Individual changes may implement improvements but do not define the entire improvement practice.","whyNl":"Continual improvement houdt practices en services passend bij veranderende behoeften. Een change kan een verbetering uitvoeren, maar change enablement heeft de specifieke focus op risico, autorisatie en planning. Herstel en configuratie-informatie zijn weer andere purposes.","hook":"An improvement may use changes; it is broader than change authorization.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-051","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Which purpose belongs to service level management rather than monitoring and event management?","options":["Setting business-based service targets and assessing delivery against them","Observing components and reporting selected significant state changes","Restoring normal operations after an unexpected service failure","Nurturing stakeholder links at strategic and tactical levels"],"why":"Service level management establishes and assesses meaningful service targets. Monitoring supplies observations, but observations alone do not define appropriate business targets.","whyNl":"Service level management spreekt betekenisvolle businessgerichte servicetargets af en beoordeelt de levering. Monitoring levert waarnemingen, maar bepaalt daarmee niet automatisch passende targets. Herstel en brede relaties horen bij andere practices.","hook":"A measurement is useful only against an appropriate service target.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-052","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset and CI","prompt":"A licensed application has financial value and must be managed to deliver a service. Which classification is supported?","options":["It can be both an IT asset and a configuration item","It must be an IT asset instead of a configuration item","It must be a configuration item instead of an IT asset","Its classification depends only on whether it is hardware or software"],"why":"The definitions overlap: financial value concerns assets and required management for delivery concerns CIs. Physical form does not make them exclusive.","whyNl":"Beide definities kunnen gelden. Financiële waarde maakt het een IT asset; moeten beheren voor servicelevering maakt het een CI. Het is geen keuze tussen hardware en software en het ene label sluit het andere niet uit.","hook":"An item can satisfy both definitions.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-053","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Known error and problem","prompt":"An investigation has been logged, but analysis of the suspected cause has not yet been performed. Which fact is still needed to describe it as a known error?","options":["The problem has been analysed and remains unresolved","The incident has received a high-priority label","A permanent change has been authorized for deployment","Several users have reported the same symptoms"],"why":"Known error requires an analysed unresolved problem. Priority, repetition or approval for a fix do not by themselves supply that analysis.","whyNl":"Een known error is een geanalyseerd, nog onopgelost problem. Logging, prioriteit of veel meldingen bewijst geen analyse. Een fix goedkeuren is evenmin de definitie. Een workaround is niet vereist om het known error te kunnen noemen.","hook":"Logged is not the same as analysed.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-054","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event and incident","prompt":"Monitoring reports a component state change important for management. The service continues normally. What can be concluded from these facts?","options":["There is an event; an incident has not been established","There is an incident because every recorded event is a failure","There is a known error because the state change was recorded","There is a problem because service quality has been reduced"],"why":"A significant state change is an event. Normal service operation does not establish interruption or degradation, and recording an event is not analysis of a cause.","whyNl":"Het event staat vast, maar een incident niet: de service draait normaal. Registreren maakt geen known error. Er is ook geen kwaliteitsvermindering beschreven die de laatste optie ondersteunt. Kijk naar bewezen feiten, niet naar wat later misschien blijkt.","hook":"Significant state change does not necessarily mean interruption.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-055","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Change definition","prompt":"Which statement identifies a change most broadly in ITIL 4?","options":["An addition, modification or removal that may affect services directly or indirectly","Only software that has already been installed in production","Only functionality already made available to end users","An interruption that reduces the quality of normal service"],"why":"A change includes potential direct or indirect service effects and is not limited to deployed code or released functionality. Interruption defines an incident.","whyNl":"Change omvat toevoegen, wijzigen of verwijderen van iets dat services kan beïnvloeden, ook indirect. Het hoeft nog niet geïnstalleerd of vrijgegeven te zijn. Een onderbreking beschrijft een incident, niet de brede definitie van change.","hook":"Potential service effect, not just deployed software.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-056","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement targets and plans","prompt":"The team knows current waiting time and agrees that it should fall to two days within three months. It has not yet chosen actions. Which step is it completing?","options":["Where do we want to be?","How do we get there?","Where are we now?","Did we get there?"],"why":"The team is specifying a measurable future state. Planning the route needs actions and resources; a baseline or evaluation describes different measurements.","whyNl":"Twee dagen binnen drie maanden is de gewenste meetbare situatie. De route is nog niet gekozen, dus niet How do we get there? De huidige wachttijd is de nulmeting; achteraf toetsen is Did we get there? Het woord termijn maakt een target nog geen plan.","hook":"A target describes the destination, not the route.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-057","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement plans and action","prompt":"A team agrees the target, then selects which tasks to perform and which resources each task needs. No tasks have been carried out. Which step is this?","options":["How do we get there?","Take action","Where do we want to be?","How do we keep the momentum going?"],"why":"Selecting and organizing the work is planning how to reach the target. Execution, defining the target and sustaining achieved gains have different purposes.","whyNl":"Werk kiezen en middelen plannen is de route uitwerken. Take action is het daadwerkelijke uitvoeren. Het target ligt al vast, dus Where do we want to be? is niet de huidige handeling. Er is ook nog geen bereikt resultaat om vast te houden.","hook":"Selecting actions is still planning them.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-058","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Baseline and evaluation","prompt":"The same performance measure is used before and after an improvement. Which pairing correctly distinguishes the model steps?","options":["Initial baseline: Where are we now?; result compared with target: Did we get there?","Initial baseline: Did we get there?; result compared with target: Where are we now?","Initial baseline: What is the vision?; result compared with target: Take action","Initial baseline: Where do we want to be?; result compared with target: How do we get there?"],"why":"Measurement is not unique to one step. Its purpose distinguishes establishing the starting point from evaluating the achieved result.","whyNl":"Beide stappen gebruiken metingen. Het doel maakt het verschil: vertrekpunt bepalen is Where are we now?; na uitvoering het resultaat aan de doelstelling toetsen is Did we get there? Alleen het woord meten herkennen is onvoldoende.","hook":"Ask why the measurement is being made.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-059","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Vision and targets","prompt":"Before setting a numerical target, the team checks which organizational objective an improvement will support. Which step does this illustrate?","options":["What is the vision?","Where do we want to be?","How do we get there?","Did we get there?"],"why":"Connecting improvement with organizational direction belongs to vision. A measurable future state, route and evaluation come from other questions.","whyNl":"De organisatierichting verklaart waarom de verbetering relevant is. Dat hoort bij vision. Een concreet meetbaar eindpunt is het toekomsttarget; een aanpak is de route. Hier is nog niets uitgevoerd om te evalueren.","hook":"Direction explains why the destination matters.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-060","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Keeping momentum","prompt":"An improvement has met its target. Which action most directly helps keep the momentum going?","options":["Reinforce the successful habits and continue seeking further improvements","Create the initial baseline for the same completed improvement","Select a target while disregarding the achieved result","Treat the successful project as the end of improvement responsibility"],"why":"Momentum concerns sustaining and building on gains. Measurement and target selection remain useful, but the described improvement already achieved its target.","whyNl":"Na bevestigd succes wil je resultaat vasthouden en verder leren. Niet doen alsof de eerste nulmeting nog ontbreekt, eerdere resultaten negeren of verbetering als afgesloten verantwoordelijkheid zien. Succes borgen is een expliciete stap.","hook":"Sustain the gain and keep improving.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-061","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement register","prompt":"An employee records an improvement idea in a continual improvement register. What does that entry establish?","options":["An opportunity is captured for assessment and prioritization","The implementation is authorized for immediate execution","The desired outcome has already been achieved","The risk assessment for the resulting change is complete"],"why":"Recording an opportunity is not approval, implementation or proof of success. The register supports managing improvement opportunities.","whyNl":"Registreren betekent dat het idee wordt vastgelegd om te beoordelen en prioriteren. Het is geen automatische toestemming, geen gerealiseerd resultaat en geen afgeronde change-risicobeoordeling. Die stappen vragen afzonderlijke beslissingen en bewijs.","hook":"Recorded does not mean approved.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-062","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement responsibilities","prompt":"Which TWO statements are correct?\n1. Staff outside a dedicated improvement team can contribute improvement ideas.\n2. Improvement work can be supported by a dedicated team.\n3. Creating a dedicated team removes improvement responsibility from everyone else.\n4. Only changes involving new technology can be improvements.","options":["1 and 2","1 and 3","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Improvement involves everyone and can be coordinated by specialists. It applies to services, practices and other elements, not only new technology.","whyNl":"1 en 2 zijn juist: iedereen kan bijdragen en een gespecialiseerd team kan ondersteunen. 3 schuift ten onrechte alle verantwoordelijkheid weg. 4 beperkt verbetering ten onrechte tot technologie; ook werkwijzen, samenwerking en services kunnen verbeteren.","hook":"Shared responsibility with coordinated support.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"contrast-063","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Standard and normal changes","prompt":"A familiar update is low risk but the proposed version falls outside the pre-authorized procedure. There is no emergency. How should it be handled?","options":["Assess, schedule and authorize it through an appropriate normal-change route","Treat it as standard because it is familiar and low risk","Treat it as emergency because the procedure does not cover it","Proceed under the old authorization and record the variation afterwards"],"why":"Standard status depends on the authorized model and conditions, not only familiarity or risk. A change outside those conditions needs suitable assessment and authorization.","whyNl":"Een bekende laagrisicotaak is niet automatisch standaard. Deze uitvoering valt buiten de vooraf toegestane voorwaarden. Zonder spoed gebruik je passende normale beoordeling en autorisatie. Een ontbrekend model maakt het geen emergency en de oude toestemming dekt de afwijking niet.","hook":"Pre-authorization has defined boundaries.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-064","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Emergency changes","prompt":"An emergency update is needed urgently. Which approach is appropriate?","options":["Use suitably expedited assessment and authorization","Omit assessment because speed makes the risk acceptable","Use pre-authorization simply because the work is urgent","Always wait for the next routine approval meeting"],"why":"Urgency changes the handling speed and controls needed, but it does not itself remove risk or create pre-authorization.","whyNl":"Spoed vraagt een passende versnelde route. Risico verdwijnt niet omdat het snel moet en urgentie levert geen voorafgaande toestemming op. Altijd wachten op een normale vergadering kan onaanvaardbare schade laten voortduren.","hook":"Expedited does not mean uncontrolled.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-065","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change authority","prompt":"What should primarily determine the appropriate change authority?","options":["The change type and level of risk under the agreed approach","The technical experience of the implementer regardless of authorization limits","The service ownership title without considering the change model","A requirement that every change use the same senior committee"],"why":"Different change models and risk levels can need different authorizing people or groups. Consistency does not require one committee for all changes.","whyNl":"De juiste authority hangt af van het soort wijziging, risico en afgesproken werkwijze. Technische ervaring alleen geeft geen autorisatie en de functietitel alleen bepaalt niet het passende niveau. Eén zeer senior commissie voor alles is ook geen ITIL-eis. De authority kan een persoon of groep zijn.","hook":"Appropriate authority, not automatically the biggest committee.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-066","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change schedule","prompt":"Two authorized changes use the same service window. What does the change schedule primarily help the teams do?","options":["Coordinate timing and identify possible conflicts","Replace the authorization decisions with one diary entry","Prove that each implementation will succeed","Remove the need for service-impact assessment"],"why":"A schedule provides visibility and coordination. It is not authorization, a guarantee of success or a substitute for risk and impact assessment.","whyNl":"De schedule maakt overlap zichtbaar zodat teams kunnen afstemmen. Een kalenderitem is geen autorisatie of bewijs van succesvol testen. Risico en impact blijven relevant, ook als beide wijzigingen afzonderlijk zijn goedgekeurd.","hook":"Scheduling supports coordination, not permission or proof.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-067","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident and problem closure","prompt":"A workaround restores normal service and the restoration is confirmed. Investigation of the cause continues. What is the best interpretation?","options":["The incident can be resolved while the problem remains under investigation","The incident and problem must remain unresolved until a permanent fix exists","The workaround converts the incident into a service request","Confirmed restoration proves the underlying cause has been eliminated"],"why":"Incident management aims at restored normal operation. That can occur before a permanent cause resolution, subject to appropriate confirmation and closure procedures.","whyNl":"Een incident kan opgelost zijn na bevestigd serviceherstel, terwijl problem management doorzoekt. De workaround bewijst geen definitieve oorzaaksoplossing. Het wordt evenmin een service request. Volg wel de afgesproken bevestigings- en afsluitprocedure.","hook":"Restore the service; keep managing the cause.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-068","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident prioritization","prompt":"An incident blocks a critical deadline for ten users; another affects a less urgent task for more users. What should guide priority?","options":["Agreed assessment of business impact and urgency","Number of affected users without considering the business activity","Which technical team can claim the quickest closure","The order of reports regardless of changes in impact"],"why":"Impact and urgency reflect business consequences. User count, effort and arrival order provide context but are not sufficient alone.","whyNl":"Kijk naar bedrijfsimpact en urgentie. Aantallen kunnen impact helpen beoordelen, maar bepalen niet zelfstandig de prioriteit. Een kritieke deadline voor een kleine groep kan zwaarder wegen. Snel kunnen sluiten of als eerste melden is geen volledige prioriteringsgrond.","hook":"Impact and urgency, not just volume.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-069","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident collaboration","prompt":"The first support team cannot restore a disrupted service with its current knowledge. Which response best supports incident management?","options":["Bring in relevant expertise while keeping restoration and communication coordinated","Keep the incident with that team until it discovers the root cause","Close the incident when a specialist accepts the investigation","Reclassify the disruption as a problem so restoration can wait"],"why":"Incident management can coordinate specialists and suppliers. Handover or root-cause investigation is not itself restored service.","whyNl":"Schakel geschikte expertise in en houd herstel en communicatie gecoördineerd. Een overdracht is geen herstel. Wachten op root cause of de classificatie veranderen mag niet het echte doel verdringen: normale service zo snel mogelijk terugbrengen.","hook":"Escalation supports restoration; it does not equal restoration.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-070","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Proactive problem management","prompt":"A supplier identifies a defect likely to cause future interruptions, but it has not yet caused an incident here. What is appropriate?","options":["Assess it as a potential problem and consider reducing the risk","Wait for an incident because potential causes cannot be problems","Record a resolved incident because no interruption is currently visible","Call it a known error solely because the supplier mentioned it"],"why":"A problem can be a potential cause. Its analysis and unresolved status determine known-error classification; no actual interruption has been established.","whyNl":"Een mogelijke oorzaak valt onder problem. Je hoeft niet op de eerste verstoring te wachten. Er is geen opgelost incident beschreven. Een melding door een supplier bewijst op zichzelf ook niet dat de analyse voor een known error gereed is.","hook":"Potential causes count too.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-071","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Known errors without workarounds","prompt":"A problem has been analysed and is still unresolved, but no workaround is available. Which statement is correct?","options":["It can be a known error without a workaround","It becomes a known error only after a workaround is documented","It cannot be a problem until normal service has been restored","It must be a normal change because analysis has finished"],"why":"Analysis plus unresolved status satisfies the known-error definition. A workaround is a possible way to limit effects, not a definitional prerequisite.","whyNl":"Geanalyseerd en nog onopgelost is voldoende. Een workaround helpt tegen de gevolgen, maar is geen voorwaarde. Een problem vereist ook niet eerst herstel. Afronding van analyse verandert de oorzaak niet automatisch in een change.","hook":"Known error: analysed, unresolved.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-072","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Managing unresolved problems","prompt":"The cost of a permanent solution exceeds the expected benefit and an effective workaround exists. What should the organization do?","options":["Assess residual risk and keep the unresolved problem and workaround under review","Mark the cause as permanently removed because users can work","Require a permanent solution regardless of costs or benefits","Stop collecting related information once the workaround is recorded"],"why":"Not every problem justifies immediate permanent correction. Costs, risks and benefits should be assessed while the unresolved condition remains managed.","whyNl":"Een definitieve oplossing hoeft niet altijd direct rendabel te zijn. Beheer het resterende risico en blijf de workaround en het problem volgen. Bruikbare omweg betekent niet dat de oorzaak weg is. Registratie is geen reden om niet meer te monitoren of beoordelen.","hook":"Accepting residual risk still requires management.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-073","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request approval","prompt":"A routine access request requires a manager's approval in its request model. How should it be fulfilled?","options":["Follow the predefined workflow, including the approval","Skip the approval because routine requests are always pre-authorized","Treat it as an incident because the access is not yet provided","Classify it as a problem because approval is a potential delay"],"why":"Predefined requests can include approvals. Routine fulfilment does not bypass authorization or turn a normal request into a disruption or cause.","whyNl":"Normale service requests mogen goedkeuringen bevatten. Het request model bepaalt de route. Routine betekent niet automatisch vooraf geautoriseerd. Nog geen nieuw recht hebben is ook niet zonder meer een verstoring van een bestaande service.","hook":"Predefined does not mean approval-free.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-074","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Requests and standard changes","prompt":"An agreed laptop request is fulfilled using a documented pre-authorized installation procedure. Which relationship is correct?","options":["Request management can coordinate fulfilment that includes a standard change","The installation removes the need for request management","Any user request makes the included change an emergency","A standard change must be re-authorized as normal each time it fulfils a request"],"why":"Practices can work together; a request can include a change executed within a pre-authorized model. The two classifications describe different aspects.","whyNl":"Request management behandelt het verzoek. Een standard change kan onderdeel zijn van die afhandeling, binnen toegestane voorwaarden. De practices vervangen elkaar niet. Een gebruikersverzoek maakt niets automatisch spoed of een normal change.","hook":"One request can include work from several practices.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-075","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk capability","prompt":"Routine work is automated and the remaining user contacts are more complex. Which capability is especially important for the service desk?","options":["Communication, empathy and understanding of the user's business context","Routing every contact without understanding what the user needs","Taking responsibility for every specialist resolution personally","Reducing conversation duration even when understanding is incomplete"],"why":"The desk remains the human contact point and needs to understand people and business context. Automation does not make empathy or coordination obsolete.","whyNl":"Juist de resterende complexe gesprekken vragen begrip, communicatie en empathie. De desk hoeft niet alles zelf technisch op te lossen. Blind routeren of gespreksduur verkorten terwijl de hulpvraag onduidelijk blijft, ondersteunt de gebruiker niet goed.","hook":"Automation leaves human understanding important.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-076","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service measures","prompt":"All component dashboards are green, but users cannot finish their business transactions within the agreed time. What should service level management do?","options":["Review end-to-end service performance and the appropriateness of the measures","Declare the service successful because each component met its own target","Replace customer feedback with a larger set of component counters","Transfer the business-outcome concern entirely to the supplier"],"why":"Component results can conceal poor end-to-end service. Targets and measures should reflect meaningful business-based service quality.","whyNl":"Groene componentcijfers bewijzen geen goede volledige service. Onderzoek de klantreis en of targets de relevante businesskwaliteit meten. Meer technische tellers vervangen gebruikerservaring niet. Verantwoordelijkheid volledig afschuiven helpt evenmin.","hook":"Component green can hide service red.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-077","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level agreements","prompt":"Which TWO characteristics support a useful service level agreement?\n1. Targets are linked to business needs.\n2. The wording is understandable to the relevant parties.\n3. Component measures replace discussion of the whole service.\n4. Every provider measure becomes a target regardless of relevance.","options":["1 and 2","1 and 3","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Business relevance and mutual understanding support useful agreements. A catalogue of technical measures is not automatically a meaningful service commitment.","whyNl":"1 en 2 zijn juist. Doelen moeten betekenis hebben voor de business en begrijpelijk zijn voor de betrokkenen. 3 vervangt de hele service door onderdelen. 4 maakt alles meetbaar belangrijk, ook als het geen relevante serviceafspraak ondersteunt.","hook":"Business-based and understood by both sides.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"}]};
